60849", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 235.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "BH-2 is a hybrid brinjal released in 1994 by Punjab Agricultural University, Ludhiana. The plants are medium, erect, spreading and thornless, with green and purplish leaves. It belongs to the round fruiting type and bears oblong, deep purple fruits that weigh 300 g on average. The fruits are highly suitable for cooking as bhartha. The yield is 235 q/acre. It is recommended for AICRP zones IV and V, with 2002 as the year of identification. It is tolerant to fruit borer.", "label_hi": "बैंगन BH-2", "label_mr": "वांगे BH-2", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "AICRP zones IV, V (year of identification 2002)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "235 q/acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "f77deee7-8c6d-4687-b274-236add1defaf", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 283.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "3254(E)", "notification_date": "2022-07-20", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Manohar is a hybrid brinjal released in 2022 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Vegetable Research, Varanasi, and notified under S.O. 3254(E) dated 2022-07-20. It comes to flowering in 48 days. The fruits are medium long and light purple to pinkish purple, with soft pulp, few seeds and a green calyx. They are suitable for curry and Kalaunji making. The yield is 650-700 q/ha. It is recommended for Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra and Goa. It is moderately resistant to Phomopsis blight and Fusarium wilt.", "label_hi": "बैंगन काशी मनोहर", "label_mr": "वांगे काशी मनोहर", "aes": {"flowering_days": "48 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Goa", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "650-700 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "471e6882-4382-4981-aeb3-c560d2ac2da0", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 214.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "1480(E)", "notification_date": "2021-04-01", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Vijay is an open-pollinated brinjal variety released in 2021 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Vegetable Research, Varanasi, and notified under S.O. 1480(E) dated 2021-04-01. The plants are bushy with sturdy stems. The fruits are medium long and purplish pink, and they are suitable for Kalaunji making. The yield is 470-530 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and Punjab. Under field conditions, it is tolerant to Phomopsis blight and Fusarium wilt.", "label_hi": "बैंगन काशी विजय", "label_mr": "वांगे काशी विजय", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand, Punjab", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "470-530 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "73de42e7-235d-4663-b8d9-1b33df7352ee", "maturity_days_min": 180, "maturity_days_max": 190, "yield_potential": 161.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Krishna is a hybrid brinjal released in 1991 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth, Rahuri, through its AICRP on Vegetable Crops centre. The crop duration is 180-190 days. The plants are tall and hardy. Fruits are borne singly and have spines on the pedicel; they are egg shaped, spiny, and purple with white stripes. The fruits are tasty. The yield is 400 q/ha. It is grown in kharif and summer and is recommended for Maharashtra, on well drained silt loam or clay loam soils rich in organic matter. It is resistant to lodging.", "label_hi": "बैंगन कृष्णा", "label_mr": "वांगे कृष्णा", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Well drained silt loam or clay loam soils rich in organic matter"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "180-190 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "400 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b285db19-c2cc-4ac8-9ba6-44a34fa6a94f", "maturity_days_min": 175, "maturity_days_max": 180, "yield_potential": 182.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Arjun is a hybrid brinjal released in 2011 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth, Rahuri, through its AICRP on Vegetable Crops centre. The crop duration is 175-180 days. The fruits are oval, tender and spiny, green with purple and white stripes, and weigh 60 g on average. The yield is 450 q/ha. It is grown in kharif and summer and is recommended for Maharashtra. It suits well drained silt loam or clay loam soils rich in organic matter.", "label_hi": "बैंगन फुले अर्जुन", "label_mr": "वांगे फुले अर्जुन", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Well drained silt loam or clay loam soils rich in organic matter"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "175-180 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "450 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3435dc86-741e-4248-9636-d24c02c9f90b", "maturity_days_min": 180, "maturity_days_max": 180, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Harit is an open-pollinated brinjal variety released in 2002 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth, Rahuri, through its AICRP on Vegetable Crops centre. The crop duration is 180 days. The fruits are pale green with white stripes at the tip, tender and less spiny, and weigh about 190 g on average. They are good for roasting to make bharta. The yield is 300 q/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for Maharashtra, on well drained silt loam or clay loam soils rich in organic matter.", "label_hi": "बैंगन फुले हरित", "label_mr": "वांगे फुले हरित", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Well drained silt loam or clay loam soils rich in organic matter"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "180 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "300 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "55e9fd40-ee6a-46d5-bfd8-80d53f93141c", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 125.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Punjab Sadabahar is an open-pollinated brinjal variety released in 1987 by Punjab Agricultural University, Ludhiana. The first harvest is at 76 days. The plants are dwarf, erect and thornless, with green leaves. It is a long fruiting type with long, thin, deep purple fruits. The yield is 125 q/acre. It is grown in summer and autumn, and also as a ratoon crop. Its year of identification under AICRP is 2001. It is comparatively tolerant to fruit borer.", "label_hi": "बैंगन पंजाब सदाबहार", "label_mr": "वांगे पंजाब सदाबहार", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "76 days", "season": "summer", "recommended_areas_published": "AICRP recommended zone printed as 'IVVI' (year of identification 2001)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "125 q/acre", "season_published": "summer, autumn, ratoon", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "c8a8a1fb-6986-48f5-91d9-c619411dbfad", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 141.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "progeny selection of cross GR x 91-2", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Ankur is an open-pollinated brinjal variety released by ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute, New Delhi. It was developed by progeny selection from the cross GR x 91-2. The first harvest is at 45-50 days. The plants are semi upright (semi erect), medium to tall (65 cm), with 6-8 branches. The fruits are small, slightly oval to oval-round, glossy and dark purple, and weigh 60-80 g. The fruits do not lose their colour and tenderness even when picking is delayed. The yield is 35.0 t/ha. It is recommended for Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra.", "label_hi": "बैंगन पूसा अंकुर", "label_mr": "वांगे पूसा अंकुर", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "45-50 days", "recommended_areas_published": "M.P. and Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "35.0 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "66822bb2-c214-4e29-90c0-fe37fe90e74a", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "progeny selection of cross GR x 91-2", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Bindu is an open-pollinated brinjal variety released by ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute, New Delhi. It was developed by progeny selection from the cross GR x 91-2. The first harvest is at 55-60 days. The plants are spineless and 55-60 cm tall, with green leaves. The fruits are small (70-75 g), slightly oval, glossy and dark purple, and are borne in clusters of 4-5. The yield is 30.0 t/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra and Gujarat.", "label_hi": "बैंगन पूसा बिंदु", "label_mr": "वांगे पूसा बिंदू", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "55-60 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra and Gujarat", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "30.0 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "9f856373-bb4e-492e-81c5-0fb664eee428", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 212.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Hybrid-20 is a hybrid brinjal released by ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute, New Delhi. The first harvest can be taken at 55 days. The plants are non-spiny and semi-erect, with light purple pigmentation partly on the younger leaves and new branches. The fruits are long, dark purple and glossy, and weigh 90-100 g. The yield is 52.5 t/ha. It is recommended for Zone-IV, covering Punjab, Delhi, Uttar Pradesh and Bihar.", "label_hi": "बैंगन पूसा हाइब्रिड-20", "label_mr": "वांगे पूसा हायब्रिड-20", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "55 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Zone-IV: Punjab, Delhi, Uttar Pradesh and Bihar", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "52.5 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "42c7c611-aa7a-4480-97fd-019dcfe06250", "maturi