ts weigh 200-250 g and larger fruits 250-300 g. The yield is 425-450 q/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra and Gujarat.", "label_hi": "बैंगन पूसा उत्तम", "label_mr": "वांगे पूसा उत्तम", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "60 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra and Gujarat", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "425-450 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "d3bb8ecb-835d-4d37-ba79-da5a626072fa", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 105, "yield_potential": 42.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Guar was released in 2016 by the AICRP on Vegetable Crops at Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. It is an open-pollinated (OPV) cluster bean variety with a crop duration of 100-105 days. Its pods are an attractive light green colour and 6 cm long, and 50 pods weigh 41 g on average. It yields 104.0 q/ha. It is suited to the kharif and summer seasons and to sandy loam soil. It is moderately resistant to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "ग्वार फली फुले ग्वार", "label_mr": "गवार फुले गवार", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam soil"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100-105 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "104.0 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "6cc9a660-cde8-4b77-ad32-deedef4f6011", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 141.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Konkan Ruchira is a drumstick variety released in 1992 by Dr. Balasaheb Sawant Konkan Krishi Vidyapeeth (DBSKKV), Dapoli. It grows into a medium-size tree with a height of 5.6 m and has dark green foliage. Its pods, also called sticks, are dark green in colour and medium long. The sticks are of the best quality. This variety gives a yield of 30-35 t/ha.", "label_hi": "सहजन कोंकण रुचिरा", "label_mr": "शेवगा कोकण रुचिरा", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "30-35 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5f743155-bed9-4de5-94ca-2e428cf97d23", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 210.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pureline selection (continuous selfing for six generations) from material collected from Eppothumvendran, Tirunelveli region", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PKM 1 was released in 1989 by Tamil Nadu Agricultural University, HC&RI Periyakulam. It is an open-pollinated annual moringa, developed by pureline selection (continuous selfing for six generations) from material collected at Eppothumvendran in the Tirunelveli region. It flowers in 5-6 months and the first harvest comes at 7-8 months; the peak harvest period is March-August. Plants reach 4-6 m height in a year with 6-12 primary branches, and ratoon crops can be maintained for 3-4 years. The pods are fleshy, 75 cm long, 6.3 cm in girth and 150 g in weight, with 70% flesh. A tree bears 220 fruits (pods) on average, and the yield is 52 t/ha.", "label_hi": "सहजन PKM 1", "label_mr": "शेवगा PKM 1", "aes": {"flowering_days": "5-6 months", "first_harvest_days": "7-8 months", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "52 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ce2b2842-ff93-4446-8b96-55baa3292d39", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 396.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "MP 31 (Eppothum vendran local) x MP 28 (Arasaradi local)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PKM 2 was released in 2000 by Tamil Nadu Agricultural University, HC&RI Periyakulam. It is an annual moringa developed from the cross MP 31 (Eppothum vendran local) x MP 28 (Arasaradi local). It comes to bearing in 6 months, and a ratoon crop can be taken for three years. The pods are 126 cm long, 8.3 cm in girth and 280 g in weight, with 70% flesh. A tree gives 220 pods per year on average, and the yield is 98 t/ha.", "label_hi": "सहजन PKM 2", "label_mr": "शेवगा PKM 2", "aes": {"duration_other": "6 months (time to bearing)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "98 tonnes/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "f936cd51-c4e8-47c9-a2dd-eee34b0b958d", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Akola Bahar is an okra (bhindi) variety released in 2004 by Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh Krishi Vidyapeeth, Akola. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) and not a hybrid. Akola Bahar has an early harvesting period, so the picking of its fruits starts early in the crop. The fruits of this variety are of less thickness, that is, they are slim in shape.", "label_hi": "भिंडी अकोला बहार", "label_mr": "भेंडी अकोला बहार", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ac4eeed6-fa56-4bc0-ae2e-0449138ef599", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 72.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Interspecific hybridization (Abelmoschus esculentus x A. manihot spp tetraphyllus var. tetraphyllus) followed by back cross breeding", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Abhay is an okra variety from ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed by interspecific hybridization (Abelmoschus esculentus x A. manihot spp tetraphyllus var. tetraphyllus) followed by back cross breeding. Its fruits are lush green, tender, long and free from spines, with a delicate aroma. They have good keeping and cooking qualities and are suitable for the fresh market as well as for canning and dehydration. The yield is 18 t/ha. It is recommended for West Bengal and Assam. It is field tolerant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी अर्का अभय", "label_mr": "भेंडी अर्का अभय", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "West Bengal and Assam", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "18 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "0078cab2-ab99-4191-b806-8d0db574fdc9", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Interspecific hybridization (Abelmoschus esculentus x A. manihot spp tetraphyllus var. tetraphyllus) followed by back cross breeding", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Anamika is an okra variety from ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed by interspecific hybridization (Abelmoschus esculentus x A. manihot spp tetraphyllus var. tetraphyllus) followed by back cross breeding. Its fruits are lush green, tender, long and free from spines, with 5-6 ridges and a delicate aroma. They have good keeping and cooking qualities. The yield is 20 t/ha. It is recommended for cultivation all over India. It is field tolerant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी अर्का अनामिका", "label_mr": "भेंडी अर्का अनामिका", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "20 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "972a731a-6e9a-4b83-8b8f-f23e0a91e8c4", "maturity_days_min": 125, "maturity_days_max": 130, "yield_potential": 97.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi"], "parentage": "GMS-4 X IIIHR-299-14-11-585 (as printed)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Nikitha is an okra hybrid released in 2024 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru, from the cross GMS-4 x IIIHR-299-14-11-585. The crop duration is 125-130 days and the first harvest is at 43 days. The first female flower appears at the 9th node from the base. In kharif, plants average 169.00 cm in height with 4.33 branches, and fruits average 12.93 cm in length and 26.5 g in weight. The fruits are dark green, medium, smooth, tender, five-ridged and free from spines. They contain iodine 33.31 µg/kg, mucilage 1.08% (fresh weight), edible fibre 8.85% (dry weight), potassium 3.7% and calcium 997 mg/100 g, and have excellent cooking quality with rich antioxidant activity. It is grown in the kharif and rabi seasons, and the yield is 21-24 t/ha. It is recommended for Karnataka and is resistant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी अर्का निकिता", "label_mr": "भेंडी अर्का निकिता", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "43 days", "season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "Karnataka", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "125-130 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "21-24 t/ha", "season_published": "kharif, rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b2507b9b-b6b1-4d98-a789-5a4baa7e514d", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 60.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": "hybrid", "description": "HBH-142 is an okra hybrid variety developed by CCS Haryana Agricultural University, Hisar. In this hybrid, fruiting starts on the third or fourth node of the plant. It is meant for the rainy season, and its yield is 135-150 q/ha. It is recommended for zones IV, V and VII of the All India Coordinated Research Project on Vegetable Crops (AICRP-VC). HBH-142 is resistant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी HBH-142", "label_mr": "भेंडी HBH-142", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "AICRP-VC zones IV, V, VII", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "135-150 q/ha", "season_published": "rainy", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "8e389302-d552-4407-b75b-a1364e0ebb92", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 60.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "2363(E)", "notification_date": "2012-10-04", "release_year": 2012, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Kranti was released in 2012 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Vegetable Research (IIVR), Varanasi, and notified under S.O. 2363(E) dated 2012-10-04. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The first harvest is at 39-41 days. Plants are medium to tall with 2-3 branches, and the first flower appears at the 5th node in the rainy season. Each plant bears 21-23 fruits on average; the fruits are dark green and 10-11 cm long. The yield is 140-150 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and Punjab. It is resistant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV) and okra leaf curl virus (OLCV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी काशी क्रांति", "label_mr": "भेंडी काशी क्रांती", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "39-41 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and Punjab", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "140-150 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1f17b915-a17c-407a-8187-d23c213a5340", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 76.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": "597(E)", "notification_date": "2006-04-25", "release_year": 2006, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Pragati was released in 2006 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Vegetable Research (IIVR), Varanasi, and notified under S.O. 597(E) dated 2006-04-25. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The first harvest is at 36-38 days. Plants are tall, 130-175 cm in height, with 1-2 effective branches. The first flower appears at the 4th node in the rainy season and at the 3rd node in summer. Each plant bears 23-25 fruits, which are 8-10 cm long at the marketable stage. The yield is 180-190 q/ha. It is grown in the rainy and summer seasons and is recommended for Chhattisgarh, Odisha and Andhra Pradesh. It is resistant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV) and okra leaf curl virus (OLCV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी काशी प्रगति", "label_mr": "भेंडी काशी प्रगती", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "36-38 days", "season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "Chhattisgarh, Odisha and A.P.", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "180-190 q/ha", "season_published": "rainy, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "6f7792ce-2d19-471b-a967-092e4dacce5c", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 125, "yield_potential": 64.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kirti is an okra (bhindi) variety released in 1999 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri, through its centre of the All India Coordinated Research Project (AICRP) on Vegetable Crops. It has a crop duration of 100-125 days. Its fruits are green with a red tinge. The yield is 160 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons and suits medium, fertile and well-drained soil.", "label_hi": "भिंडी कीर्ति", "label_mr": "भेंडी कीर्ती", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium, fertile and well drained"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100-125 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "160 q /ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "40765fc9-54ef-40f2-b3ff-9dd191af5e72", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pusa Sawani x Abelmoschus manihot (YVM-resistant wild species), two backcrosses to Pusa Sawani, then selection in selfing generations", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Parbhani Kranti was developed by Marathwada Agricultural University, Parbhani (now VNMKV). It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) bred from the cross Pusa Sawani x Abelmoschus manihot, a wild species resistant to yellow vein mosaic, followed by two backcrosses to Pusa Sawani and then selection in the selfing generations. The first harvest is at 45-50 days. Plants are tall and single-stemmed with dark green foliage. The fruits are extremely dark green, smooth, tender and slender, with a marketable length of 8 to 9 cm. It is resistant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी परभणी क्रांति", "label_mr": "भेंडी परभणी क्रांती", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "45-50 days", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "833136a5-9518-4b44-be1f-b8a8e65b6874", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 95.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Gayatri was released in 2025 by the Vegetable Improvement Project, Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) with a crop duration of 110-120 days. The fruits are medium in size, 10-15 cm long and 10-12 g in weight, attractive green and without seediness. The yield is 234.64 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons, suits medium, fertile and well-drained soil, and is recommended for Western Maharashtra. It is moderately resistant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV) and to the pests fruit borer and whitefly.", "label_hi": "भिंडी फुले गायत्री", "label_mr": "भेंडी फुले गायत्री", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium, fertile and well drained"], "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "234.64 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3e2e8782-6d60-479f-923a-2783634512c5", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 93.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Utkarsha was released in 2003 by NARP Ganeshkhind, Pune, of Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) with a crop duration of 110-120 days. Its fruits are dark green with five ridges, tender, attractive and shining, and straight and slender in shape. The yield is 220-230 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons, suits medium, fertile and well-drained soil, and is recommended for Western Maharashtra.", "label_hi": "भिंडी फुले उत्कर्षा", "label_mr": "भेंडी फुले उत्कर्षा", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium, fertile and well drained"], "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "220-230 q /ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5f0360da-458c-4b26-8e0e-e3f197552ca3", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 85.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Vimukta was released in 2016 by NARP Ganeshkhind, Pune, of Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) with a crop duration of 110-120 days. Its fruits are attractive green and shining. The yield is 200-210 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons, suits medium, fertile and well-drained soil, and is recommended for Western Maharashtra. It is resistant to yellow vein mosaic virus (YVMV).", "label_hi": "भिंडी फुले विमुक्ता", "label_mr": "भेंडी फुले विमुक्ता", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium, fertile and well drained"], "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "200-210 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "05af6bab-1863-44f7-a279-2acccb29379d", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 161.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2005, "variety_class": "hybrid", "description": "KGMR-1 is a cabbage hybrid released in 2005 by the ICAR-IARI Regional Station, Katrain. It forms heads in 60 days. The leaves are medium waxy, green and slightly serrated. The head is round, compact, green and covered, with crimping on the outer leaves. After maturity, the crop can stay in the field for 20 days. The yield is 350-400 q/ha. It is recommended for Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Himachal Pradesh and Uttarakhand, and for AICRP-VC zones I and IV.", "label_hi": "पत्ता गोभी KGMR-1", "label_mr": "कोबी KGMR-1", "aes": {"heading_days": "60 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Punjab, U.P., Bihar, H.P. and Uttarakhand (Checklist); AICRP-VC zones I, IV (AICRP report, see release quote)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "350-400 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ca966246-58da-4cc0-a0c4-d3d0120bad86", "maturity_days_min": 75, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 133.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Ageti is an open-pollinated (OPV) cabbage variety released by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It is a tropical type and is ready for harvest in 75-90 days. It forms marketable heads at 15-30°C, and the day temperature should not be above 35°C. The head weighs 600-1200 g. It also produces seed under sub-tropical conditions. The yield is 110-330 q/ha. It is recommended for cultivation all over India.", "label_hi": "पत्ता गोभी पूसा अगेती", "label_mr": "कोबी पूसा अगेती", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "75-90 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "110-330 q/ha", "season_published": "March planting (northern plains), August-October planting (northern plains)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5862789d-cf08-4831-9f5f-faebeaa961af", "maturity_days_min": 80, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Drum Head is an open-pollinated (OPV) cabbage variety released by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It is a late-season variety and needs a long winter for a good crop. It is ready for harvest in 80-90 days. The head is large, flat, somewhat loose and drum shaped, weighing 3-4 kg (range 3-5 kg). The cover leaves are light green, and the outer leaves are light green with a prominent mid-rib. The yield is 300 q/ha. It is resistant to black leg disease and is recommended for cultivation all over India.", "label_hi": "पत्ता गोभी पूसा ड्रम हेड", "label_mr": "कोबी पूसा ड्रम हेड", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "80-90 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "300 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b952d178-5f8c-4cec-b4ce-b1ed5253653b", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 182.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Hybrid-1 is a cabbage hybrid released by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It forms heads in 60 days. The plant has few (12-14) serrated non-wrapper leaves, and the leaves are medium waxy, green and slightly serrated. The head is round, compact, green and covered. It has better staying capacity in the field after maturity. The yield is 42-45 t/ha.", "label_hi": "पत्ता गोभी पूसा हाइब्रिड-1", "label_mr": "कोबी पूसा हायब्रिड-1", "aes": {"heading_days": "60 days", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "42-45 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "98614f72-ac12-4e99-b0fa-562fe7df0d26", "maturity_days_min": 60, "maturity_days_max": 65, "yield_potential": 176.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Hybrid-81 is a cabbage hybrid released by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It matures in 60-65 days. The plant is 22-25 cm tall and has 12-14 dark green, waxy, non-wrapping leaves. The head is round, very compact and covered with an outer leaf. After head formation, it can stay in the field for 25-30 days, which is a very good staying capacity. The yield is 43.5 t/ha. It shows field tolerance to black rot disease.", "label_hi": "पत्ता गोभी पूसा हाइब्रिड-81", "label_mr": "कोबी पूसा हायब्रिड-81", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "60-65 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "43.5 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "86b60729-38d0-47af-9125-3b5c4508cc64", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 75, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "EC 24855 × EC 10109 (developed by hybridization)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1989, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Mukta is an open-pollinated (OPV) cabbage variety released in 1989 by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It was developed by hybridization from the cross EC 24855 × EC 10109. It is ready for harvest in 70-75 days. The plant has a short stalk and light green leaves with slightly wavy margins. The head is flattish round and medium in size, with light green outer leaves, and weighs 1.5-2 kg. The yield is 300 q/ha. It is resistant to black rot and bacterial rot. It is recommended for Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, West Bengal and Assam.", "label_hi": "पत्ता गोभी पूसा मुक्ता", "label_mr": "कोबी पूसा मुक्ता", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Punjab, U.P., Bihar, W.B. and Assam", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70-75 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "300 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "820d7fd8-cc76-457b-894f-1345451c13ad", "maturity_days_min": 65, "maturity_days_max": 75, "yield_potential": 64.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "mass pedigree method of selection from IIHR Acc.No.21957", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Spoorthi is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released by the ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It was developed by the mass pedigree method of selection from IIHR Acc.No.21957. It belongs to the early maturity group and is ready for harvest in 65-75 days. It gives compact white curds. It has good seed set under tropical conditions. The yield is 15-16 t/ha. It is moderately resistant to downy mildew and Alternaria leaf spot.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी अर्का स्फूर्ति", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी अर्का स्फूर्ती", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "65-75 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "15-16 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "8f03aeec-c187-4567-b2fd-54610b8684d7", "maturity_days_min": 75, "maturity_days_max": 80, "yield_potential": 72.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "mass pedigree method of selection from IIHR Acc.No.21250", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Vimal is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released by the ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It was developed by the mass pedigree method of selection from IIHR Acc.No.21250. It belongs to the early maturity group and is ready for harvest in 75-80 days. It gives compact creamy white curds. It has good seed set under tropical conditions. The yield is 17-18 t/ha. It is moderately resistant to downy mildew and Alternaria leaf spot.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी अर्का विमल", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी अर्का विमल", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "75-80 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "17-18 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "f86ee826-75eb-4fd9-8eff-8692042f641f", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2002, "variety_class": "hybrid", "description": "DCH-541 is a cauliflower hybrid. It was released in 2002 by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It is recommended for zones II and IV of the All India Coordinated Research Project on Vegetable Crops (AICRP-VC).", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी DCH-541", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी DCH-541", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "AICRP-VC zones II, IV", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2deae77f-d26e-45dd-ab0b-1df3af126c30", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 113.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Gobhi-25 is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released in 2019 by the ICAR-Indian Institute of Vegetable Research (IIVR), Varanasi. It was notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. It is an Indian (tropical) cauliflower of the November maturity group, maturing in the first fortnight of November at around 25°C. The curd is white, compact and hemispherical, and free from riceyness, leafiness and fuzziness. The marketable curd weighs 600-700 g. The yield is 250-280 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी काशी गोभी-25", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी काशी गोभी-25", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "250-280 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "4ff45870-ff50-43f0-912f-1ae23bc10a44", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 141.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Kunwari is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released by the ICAR-Indian Institute of Vegetable Research (IIVR), Varanasi. It belongs to the early maturity group. The curd is semi-dome type, white and compact, with fine texture, and weighs about 300-450 g. The yield is 300-350 q/ha. It can tolerate heavy rainfall. It is recommended for Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar and Jharkhand.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी काशी कुंवारी", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी काशी कुंवारी", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Punjab, U.P., Bihar and Jharkhand", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "300-350 q/ha", "season_published": "sowing end of June to July (North Indian plains)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "01fb484c-1a49-44bd-9d18-d131c8dc2b6d", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 186.2, "yield_rainfed": 9.6, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Betakesari is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. The plant is semi-self-blanching. The curd is orange in colour, compact and very attractive. The marketable curd weighs about 1.250 kg. The curd contains 800-1000 µg/100 g of beta carotene. The yield is 42.0-46.0 t/ha. It is recommended for the National Capital Region.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी पूसा बीटाकेसरी", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी पूसा बीटाकेसरी", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "National Capital Region", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "42.0-46.0 t/ha", "season_published": "September – January growing period", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "916cd973-58e4-4b62-a8ab-969095b52eee", "maturity_days_min": 96, "maturity_days_max": 96, "yield_potential": 64.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2004, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Kartik Sankar is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released in 2004 by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It belongs to the early maturity group and matures in 96 days. Its curd forms at 22-25°C. The curd is compact, white and medium in size, weighing about 475 g. The yield is 145-160 q/ha. It is resistant to downy mildew. It is recommended for West Bengal, Assam, Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar and Jharkhand.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी पूसा कार्तिक संकर", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी पूसा कार्तिक संकर", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "West Bengal, Assam, Punjab, U.P., Bihar and Jharkhand", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "96 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "145-160 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "6b991789-abb2-4753-808a-4f2a3450aa12", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Shubra is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It takes 125-130 days to heading. The plant is erect with a long stalk and has bluish green leaves. The best temperature for the curd is 12-16°C. The curd is compact and white, weighing 700-800 g. The yield is 250-300 q/ha. It is resistant to black rot. It is recommended for Delhi, Punjab, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Bihar.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी पूसा शुभ्रा", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी पूसा शुभ्रा", "aes": {"heading_days": "125-130 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Delhi, Punjab, Haryana, U.P. and Bihar", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "250-300 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "40de757f-6f35-43a4-a84a-d885c39f937b", "maturity_days_min": 90, "maturity_days_max": 95, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Snowball K-1 is an open-pollinated (OPV) cauliflower variety released by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It belongs to the snowball group and is the last in this group to form curd, which extends its availability period by about a fortnight. It matures in 90-95 days. The curd is snow white and self-blanched. The yield is 300 q/ha. It is resistant to black rot and is recommended for cultivation all over India.", "label_hi": "फूलगोभी पूसा स्नोबॉल K-1", "label_mr": "फुलकोबी पूसा स्नोबॉल K-1", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "90-95 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "300 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "0be79a7b-7f5f-4809-99df-162593b16072", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 110, "yield_potential": 48.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pure line selection from the local collection IIHR-4 (from Rajasthan)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1986, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Harit is an open-pollinated bitter gourd variety released by ICAR-IIHR Bengaluru in 1986. It is a pure line selection from the local collection IIHR-4, which came from Rajasthan. The crop duration is 100-110 days. The vine is thin, with light green, deeply lobed leaves. Fruits are medium-sized and spindle shaped, with glossy green skin, smooth regular ribs and no tubercles. The flesh is thick and the fruits have fewer seeds. Bitterness is moderate. The yield is 12 t/ha. It is recommended for Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala.", "label_hi": "करेला अर्का हरित", "label_mr": "कारले अर्का हरित", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100-110 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "12 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a62eba7f-4fd8-414c-8535-f22b8f85d642", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 89.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "zaid"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Mayuri is an open-pollinated bitter gourd variety released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi in 2019 and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. It is of medium maturity. Fruits are dark green and uniform in shape and size, 20-25 cm long and weigh 80-100 g. They have comparatively fewer seeds, 10-15 per fruit. Fruits have a longer shelf life and are suitable for distant markets. The yield is 200-220 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and zaid seasons and is recommended for Uttar Pradesh. It is tolerant to anthracnose, downy mildew and mosaic virus, and tolerant to powdery mildew and fruit fly under field conditions. It can bear fruit during hot summer above 35°C.", "label_hi": "करेला काशी मयूरी", "label_mr": "कारले काशी मयूरी", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "200-220 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, zaid", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "265006d5-2c56-4c78-b71a-317f8b1f274b", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 101.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Konkan Tara is an open-pollinated bitter gourd variety released by Dr. BSKKV Dapoli in 1993. Fruits are green in colour, medium long (15-16 cm) and spindle shaped, with raised tubercles on the surface. They have good keeping quality, with a shelf life of 7-8 days at ambient (room) temperature. The yield is 23.0-25.0 t/ha. It is recommended for the Konkan region of Maharashtra.", "label_hi": "करेला कोंकण तारा", "label_mr": "कारले कोकण तारा", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Konkan region of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "23.0-25.0 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ef43dbba-b112-4adc-8c9f-a16257d30e99", "maturity_days_min": 150, "maturity_days_max": 180, "yield_potential": 101.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": "Cross Green Long x Delhi Local followed by pedigree selection (code RHRBG-5)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Green Gold is an open-pollinated bitter gourd variety released in 1996 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. It was developed from the cross Green Long x Delhi Local followed by pedigree selection (code RHRBG-5). The crop duration is 150-180 days. Fruits are dark green, 20-22 cm long, with prominent prickles. The yield is 225-250 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Maharashtra. The suitable soil is sandy loam rich in organic matter. It is tolerant to downy mildew.", "label_hi": "करेला फुले ग्रीन गोल्ड", "label_mr": "कारले फुले ग्रीन गोल्ड", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam rich in organic matter"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "150-180 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "225-250 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "e7be0ce1-3786-49da-915b-ef91dc4f50b0", "maturity_days_min": 180, "maturity_days_max": 180, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": "RHRBG-5 x RHRBG-4", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Priyanka is a hybrid bitter gourd released in 1999 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. Its parents are RHRBG-5 x RHRBG-4. The crop duration is 180 days. The foliage is dark green. Fruits are dark green, 20-22 cm long, with a highly prickled surface carrying prominent prickles. The yield is 200 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Maharashtra. The suitable soil is sandy loam rich in organic matter. It is tolerant to downy mildew.", "label_hi": "करेला फुले प्रियंका", "label_mr": "कारले फुले प्रियांका", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam rich in organic matter"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "180 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "200 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "48b5652e-7103-49af-9fc9-d51f8334ac44", "maturity_days_min": 180, "maturity_days_max": 180, "yield_potential": 59.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Ujwala is an open-pollinated bitter gourd variety released in 1999 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. The crop duration is 180 days. Fruits are dark green, medium in length and prickled. They have excellent shelf life and are suitable for long-distance markets. The yield is 147 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons, and the suitable soil is sandy loam rich in organic matter. It is tolerant to downy mildew.", "label_hi": "करेला फुले उज्ज्वला", "label_mr": "कारले फुले उज्ज्वला", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam rich in organic matter"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "180 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "147 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a5b9969b-5205-42c9-b12e-fb30ec197865", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 70.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Punjab Kareli-1 is an open-pollinated variety of bitter gourd. It was released by PAU Ludhiana in 2009. The plant has long vines, and its leaves are green, smooth and serrated. The fruits are long and thin, green in colour and ridged on the surface. Each fruit weighs about 50 g. The first harvest of fruits can be taken in 66 days. The yield of this variety is 70 q/acre.", "label_hi": "करेला पंजाब करेली-1", "label_mr": "कारले पंजाब करेली-1", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "66 days", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "70 q/acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "9ad1fc66-5d5f-4cbe-b1ad-1f056ee7efbf", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pusa Vishesh x Pusa Do Mausami (inbreds; heterosis breeding)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2002, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Hybrid-2 is a hybrid bitter gourd released by ICAR-IARI New Delhi in 2002. It was developed through heterosis breeding from the inbreds Pusa Vishesh x Pusa Do Mausami. The first harvest is ready in 55-60 days. Fruits are medium long, thick and glossy green. They are suitable for pickling and dehydration. The yield is 190-200 q/ha. It is recommended for Punjab, U.P., Bihar, Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh, Odisha, A.P., Rajasthan, Gujarat, Haryana and Delhi.", "label_hi": "करेला पूसा हाइब्रिड-2", "label_mr": "कारले पूसा हायब्रिड-2", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "55-60 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Punjab, U.P., Bihar, Jharkhand, Chhattisgarh, Odisha, A.P., Rajasthan, Gujarat, Haryana and Delhi", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "190-200 q/ha", "season_published": "spring summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5060a428-1075-453e-9988-95649bb83404", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 182.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pure line selection from IIHR-20A", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Bahar is an open-pollinated bottle gourd variety released by ICAR-IIHR Bengaluru. It is a pure line selection from IIHR-20A. Fruits are medium long and straight, without crookneck, with light green skin that shines when tender. The fruit weight is 1 kg. The yield is 40-45 t/ha. It is recommended for cultivation in M.P. and Maharashtra. It is tolerant to blossom end rot.", "label_hi": "लौकी अर्का बहार", "label_mr": "दुधी भोपळा अर्का बहार", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "M.P. and Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "40-45 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "31d76749-4006-4d78-b8fd-ed8ef2a61ec8", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 222.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "IC-92465 x DVBG-151", "notification_number": "597(E)", "notification_date": "2006-04-25", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Ganga is an open-pollinated bottle gourd variety released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi in 2006 and notified under S.O. 597(E) dated 2006-04-25. It was developed from the cross IC-92465 x DVBG-151. It is an early variety. Fruits are light green in colour, 30 cm long and 7 cm in diameter, and each fruit weighs 800-900 g. The yield is 480-550 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "लौकी काशी गंगा", "label_mr": "दुधी भोपळा काशी गंगा", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "480-550 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1bb18535-844c-43da-960e-72d427929cd3", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 210.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "1362(E)", "notification_date": "2024-03-12", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Shubhra is an open-pollinated bottle gourd variety released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi in 2024 and notified under S.O. 1362(E) dated 2024-03-12. Fruits are of the Gutka type, cylindrical, attractive green and medium long (28-30 cm). They are suitable for packaging, distant transport and export. The yield is 470-520 q/ha. It is recommended for Bihar, Jharkhand, Punjab and Uttar Pradesh. It is tolerant to downy mildew.", "label_hi": "लौकी काशी शुभ्रा", "label_mr": "दुधी भोपळा काशी शुभ्रा", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Bihar, Jharkhand, Punjab and Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "470-520 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1ef26e6c-d5a5-472b-a537-25c13631b732", "maturity_days_min": 152, "maturity_days_max": 152, "yield_potential": 167.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Gaurav is an open-pollinated bottle gourd variety released by MPKV Rahuri in 2024. The crop duration is 152 days. Fruits are green, cylindrical and medium long (27 to 30 cm), and each fruit weighs 540 to 550 g. The yield is 413.63 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Maharashtra. Medium to deep, well-drained soil is suitable for it.", "label_hi": "लौकी फुले गौरव", "label_mr": "दुधी भोपळा फुले गौरव", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium to deep, well drained"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "152 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "413.63 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "e8c186cf-f67d-4e1f-a816-db681c9282a8", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 226.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Punjab Barkat is an open-pollinated variety of bottle gourd. It was released by PAU Ludhiana in 2014. The plants are vigorous in growth and profusely branched, and the stem is hairy (pubescent). The fruits are long and cylindrical, light green in colour, shining and tender. The yield of this variety is 226 q/acre. It is moderately resistant to mosaic virus disease.", "label_hi": "लौकी पंजाब बरकत", "label_mr": "दुधी भोपळा पंजाब बरकत", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "226 q/acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a533ca68-a147-43e6-ad0f-6e6b1f50ce44", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 161.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Naveen is an open-pollinated variety of bottle gourd released by ICAR-IARI New Delhi. The fruits are cylindrical and straight in shape, and the variety is free from crook-necked fruits. Each fruit weighs 550 g. The yield of this variety is 350-400 q/ha. It is suited to the spring-summer and rainy seasons, and it is recommended for cultivation in Maharashtra and M.P.", "label_hi": "लौकी पूसा नवीन", "label_mr": "दुधी भोपळा पूसा नवीन", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra and M.P.", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "350-400 q/ha", "season_published": "spring-summer, rainy", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "eb6521ea-7d41-499a-90d7-e68e18001d93", "maturity_days_min": 150, "maturity_days_max": 180, "yield_potential": 202.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Samrat is an open-pollinated bottle gourd variety released in 1992 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. The crop duration is 150-180 days. Fruits are 30-40 cm long, perfectly cylindrical and green, with dense hairs (pubescence) on the surface. They have good keeping quality and are good for box packing. The yield is 400-500 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Maharashtra. Sandy loam soil is suitable for it.", "label_hi": "लौकी सम्राट", "label_mr": "दुधी भोपळा सम्राट", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam soil"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "150-180 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "400-500 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "174f0a44-8eeb-4173-b3cc-35fb2773d8b2", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 110, "yield_potential": 76.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Himangi is an open-pollinated cucumber variety released in 1992 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. Its crop duration is 100-110 days. The fruits are white in colour, are resistant to bronzing and have a good shelf life. The yield is 190 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Maharashtra. It suits well-drained, fertile soil.", "label_hi": "खीरा हिमांगी", "label_mr": "काकडी हिमांगी", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Well drained fertile soil"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100-110 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "190 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "55c3f6f3-d9f9-47e9-81b4-7686461b5ae2", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 74.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Nutan is a cucumber hybrid released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 5 February 2019. Its fruits are long and cylindrical in shape. The fruit colour is light green, with mottling on the peduncle (stalk) side of the fruit. The yield is 165-185 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Uttar Pradesh. The hybrid is resistant to downy mildew.", "label_hi": "खीरा काशी नूतन", "label_mr": "काकडी काशी नूतन", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "165-185 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5f3343e1-e87d-4f8f-a2af-b59118c102aa", "maturity_days_min": 90, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 145.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Prachi is an open-pollinated cucumber variety released in 2001 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. Its crop duration is 90 days. The variety is suitable for greenhouse cultivation. The fruits are yellowish white in colour. The variety gives a yield of 360 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons, and it is suited to well-drained, fertile soil.", "label_hi": "खीरा फुले प्राची", "label_mr": "काकडी फुले प्राची", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Well drained fertile soil"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "90 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "360 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2ddeaac7-83c9-483a-9f2f-6c06b764a08e", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 110, "yield_potential": 72.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Shubhangi is an open-pollinated cucumber variety released in 1999 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. Its crop duration is 100-110 days. The plant has a light green stem. The fruits are green, with a smooth surface carrying fine hairs (trichomes). The yield is 180 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons, is recommended for Maharashtra and suits well-drained, fertile soil. It is tolerant to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "खीरा फुले शुभांगी", "label_mr": "काकडी फुले शुभांगी", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Well drained fertile soil"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100-110 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "180 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "083c8cdd-a564-4d1a-bef2-6c87d7077222", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 304.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Punjab Kheera-1 is an open-pollinated cucumber variety released in 2018 by PAU Ludhiana. It is suitable for poly-net house cultivation only. It gives its first harvest in 45 days. The plants are vigorous, bear parthenocarpic flowers and carry 1-2 fruits per node. The fruits are dark green, seedless and medium sized (125 g), 13-15 cm long, free of bitterness, and do not require peeling. The yield is 304 q/acre.", "label_hi": "खीरा पंजाब खीरा-1", "label_mr": "काकडी पंजाब खीरा-1", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "45 days", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "304 q/acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ef17ae6d-fba3-4591-b9f0-37a98a4930a3", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Japanese gynoecious line × Green Long Naples", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Sanyog is a cucumber variety released by ICAR-IARI New Delhi. Its parentage is a Japanese gynoecious line × Green Long Naples. It is very early and gives its first harvest in 50 days. The fruits are cylindrical, 28-30 cm long and dark green with yellow spines, with crisp flesh. The yield is 200 q/ha. It is recommended for Himachal Pradesh, Jammu and Kashmir, and Uttarakhand.", "label_hi": "खीरा पूसा संयोग", "label_mr": "काकडी पूसा संयोग", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "50 days", "recommended_areas_published": "H.P., J&K and Uttarakhand", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "200 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "0d1b88db-4f1b-49dd-91a0-4547dbd4b2ac", "maturity_days_min": 95, "maturity_days_max": 105, "yield_potential": 101.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Sheetal is an open-pollinated cucumber variety of the early type, released in 1984 by Dr. BSKKV Dapoli. Its crop duration is 95-105 days. The plant has a high yielding vine with dark green foliage. The fruits are medium long and cylindrical in shape and green in colour. The fruits have good keeping quality. The variety gives a yield of 20-25 t/ha.", "label_hi": "खीरा शीतल", "label_mr": "काकडी शीतल", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "95-105 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "20-25 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1e765260-b09c-4ee6-b252-82b20ca9fc92", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 133.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pure line selection from IIHR-105", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Chandan is an open-pollinated pumpkin variety released by ICAR-IIHR Bengaluru. It is a pure line selection from IIHR-105. The fruits are round with a pressed blossom end and weigh 2-3 kg. The rind is green with white patches when immature and turns light brown with self-coloured patches on maturity. The flesh is thick and orange, and the cavity is solid. It is rich in carotene (3333 IU). The yield is 33 t/ha.", "label_hi": "कद्दू अर्का चंदन", "label_mr": "भोपळा अर्का चंदन", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "33 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "6a1ba52a-368a-4dcb-a42e-e9435a0d4093", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 137.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pure line selection from IIHR-79", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Suryamukhi is an open-pollinated pumpkin variety released by ICAR-IIHR Bengaluru. It is a pure line selection from IIHR-79. The fruits are round with pressed ends and weigh 1 kg on average. When mature, the rind is orange red with white stripes. The fruit stalk is round with flared ends. The yield is 34 t/ha. The variety is resistant to fruit fly.", "label_hi": "कद्दू अर्का सूर्यमुखी", "label_mr": "भोपळा अर्का सूर्यमुखी", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "34 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3dab92b2-9b31-490d-92b4-c5f0c76b5cfc", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 161.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "3254(E)", "notification_date": "2022-07-20", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Basant is an open-pollinated pumpkin variety released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi in 2022 and notified under S.O. 3254(E) dated 20 July 2022. It is early maturing and bears 3.0–4.5 fruits per plant. The fruits are round and mottled green, medium in size, weighing 2.5–3.0 kg, with a flesh thickness of 3.0–3.25 cm. The carotenoid content is 2.6 mg/100 g. The yield is 350-400 q/ha. It is recommended for Chhattisgarh, Odisha and Andhra Pradesh. It is tolerant to mosaic virus and downy mildew.", "label_hi": "कद्दू काशी बसंत", "label_mr": "भोपळा काशी बसंत", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Chhattisgarh, Odisha and Andhra Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "350-400 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "9fc75f51-03c9-4ab3-a2ca-6bb0827fb77a", "maturity_days_min": 65, "maturity_days_max": 65, "yield_potential": 141.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": ["summer", "kharif"], "parentage": "NDPK-24 x PKM, pedigree selection", "notification_number": "597(E)", "notification_date": "2006-04-25", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Harit is an open-pollinated pumpkin variety released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi in 2006 and notified under S.O. 597(E) dated 25 April 2006. It was developed by pedigree selection from the cross NDPK-24 x PKM. It is early maturing, with a crop duration of 65 days. The vine is short and the leaves are dark green with white spots. The fruits are green and spherical, weighing 2.5–3.0 kg at the green stage, and the variety is best suited for green fruit production. The yield is 300-350 q/ha. It is grown in the summer and kharif seasons and is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "कद्दू काशी हरित", "label_mr": "भोपळा काशी हरित", "aes": {"season": "summer", "recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "65 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "300-350 q/ha", "season_published": "summer, kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "64ef6934-811f-4554-87c4-f24c16263b3f", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 170.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": ["summer", "kharif"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Shishir is a pumpkin hybrid released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi in 2019 and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 5 February 2019. It is early maturing and bears 3–4 fruits per plant. The fruits are small and round, mottled green in colour and weigh 2.2–2.5 kg. The yield is 380-420 q/ha. It is grown in the summer and kharif seasons and is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "कद्दू काशी शिशिर", "label_mr": "भोपळा काशी शिशिर", "aes": {"season": "summer", "recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "380-420 q/ha", "season_published": "summer, kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "d7618253-0d24-433e-876e-0265e7d76f0b", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 206.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PPH-1 is a pumpkin hybrid released by PAU Ludhiana in 2016. It is extra-early in maturity. The vine is dwarf with a short internodal length, and the leaves are dark green. The fruits are small and round, mottled green at the immature stage and mottled brown at the mature stage. The fruit cavity is small and the flesh is golden yellow. The yield is 206 q/acre.", "label_hi": "कद्दू PPH-1", "label_mr": "भोपळा PPH-1", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "206 q/acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "4dae7768-6e5d-4804-be5c-e0caf7ac1aae", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 165.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Punjab Samrat is an open-pollinated pumpkin variety released by PAU Ludhiana in 2008. It is early in maturity. The vine is medium long, the stem is angular and the leaves are dark green. The fruits are medium in size and nearly round, mottled green in colour and turning pale brown at maturity. The flesh is thick and golden-yellow and is rich in vitamin A. The yield is 165 q/acre.", "label_hi": "कद्दू पंजाब सम्राट", "label_mr": "भोपळा पंजाब सम्राट", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "165 q/acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "671cde16-c230-4e28-a54a-947a71508f89", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 115, "yield_potential": 40.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Advanced pedigree selection of the cross T3 (from Rajasthan) x T8 (from Punjab)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Tinda is a tinda variety released by ICAR-IIHR Bengaluru. It is an advanced pedigree selection from the cross T3 (from Rajasthan) x T8 (from Punjab). Its crop duration is 110-115 days. The stem is hairy and angular, the leaves are dark green, deeply lobed and hairy, and the ovary is hairy. The fruits are round, with lush green, shining skin covered with soft hair when young and tender, and weigh 60 g at the young, tender stage. The yield is 10 t/ha.", "label_hi": "टिंडा अर्का टिंडा", "label_mr": "टिंडा अर्का टिंडा", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-115 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "adc02273-ee70-4bb8-b26f-49537d09b308", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 72.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Punjab Tinda-1 is an open-pollinated tinda variety released by PAU Ludhiana in 2018. It is early maturing and gives its first harvest in 54 days. The leaves are green and moderately lobed. The fruits are round, with a shining, green, hairy (pubescent) surface, and the flesh is white. The fruits weigh 60 g on average at the immature stage. The yield is 72 q/acre.", "label_hi": "टिंडा पंजाब टिंडा-1", "label_mr": "टिंडा पंजाब टिंडा-1", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "54 days", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "72 q/acre", "season_published": "spring", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a027d870-684c-45ed-9691-dce21751f2ee", "maturity_days_min": 140, "maturity_days_max": 150, "yield_potential": 101.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "selection from local type of Tamil Nadu", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1971, "variety_class": null, "description": "CO 1 is an ash gourd variety released by TNAU Coimbatore in 1971. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed as a selection from a local type of Tamil Nadu. The crop duration is 140-150 days. Fruits are large, green and ash coated, globular and oblong oval in shape, and each fruit weighs 6–8 kg. The yield is 25 t/ha. It is recommended for Tamil Nadu.", "label_hi": "पेठा CO 1", "label_mr": "कोहळा CO 1", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Tamil Nadu", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "140-150 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "25 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "c272cc2d-7439-45a9-ae6d-50613e695c6f", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 130, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Selection from Coimbatore local", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1982, "variety_class": null, "description": "CO 2 is an ash gourd variety released by TNAU Coimbatore in 1982. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed as a selection from Coimbatore local. The crop duration is 120-130 days. It is small fruited; fruit weight is 2-3 kg, within a range of 2-4 kg. Fruits are oblong or cylindrical in shape and compressed on both sides. The yield is 20 t/ha. It is recommended for Tamil Nadu.", "label_hi": "पेठा CO 2", "label_mr": "कोहळा CO 2", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Tamil Nadu", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-130 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "20 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "bf532860-466d-4bb9-8988-8c21d39dfde7", "maturity_days_min": 130, "maturity_days_max": 140, "yield_potential": 246.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Ujjawal is an ash gourd variety released by ICAR-Indian Institute of Vegetable Research (ICAR-IIVR), Varanasi. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The total crop duration is 130-140 days. Its fruits are globular in shape and less seeded, and each fruit weighs 10-12 kg. The yield is 600-610 q/ha. This variety is recommended for cultivation in Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala.", "label_hi": "पेठा काशी उज्ज्वल", "label_mr": "कोहळा काशी उज्ज्वल", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Punjab, U.P., Bihar, Jharkhand, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "130-140 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "600-610 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "4ebadddc-330c-4f35-a31d-bcdecbd0b500", "maturity_days_min": 145, "maturity_days_max": 145, "yield_potential": 120.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PAG-3 is an ash gourd variety released by PAU Ludhiana (Punjab Agricultural University) in 2003. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The crop is ready for harvest in 145 days. The vine is medium long and has green leaves. The fruits are attractive, globular and medium sized, with an average fruit weight of 10 kg. This variety gives a yield of 120 q/acre.", "label_hi": "पेठा PAG-3", "label_mr": "कोहळा PAG-3", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "145 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "120 q/acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5ab42e1c-6e46-49cc-992c-a351e98123c3", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 202.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": "selection from indigenous material", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Ujjwal is an ash gourd variety released by ICAR-IARI New Delhi. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed as a selection from indigenous material. The vine is medium long (3-4 m). Fruits are oblong ellipsoid with a greenish white rind and white flesh, and the average fruit weight is 7.0 kg. The fruits are ideal for long distance transportation and have long storability, keeping for more than 6 months at room temperature. The yield is 480-500 q/ha. It is suited to the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala.", "label_hi": "पेठा पूसा उज्ज्वल", "label_mr": "कोहळा पूसा उज्ज्वल", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "480-500 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "565d1493-4e78-489d-a3c2-9bf1ba9ef80d", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 89.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Amulya is a pointed gourd variety released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. Its fruits are fleshy and attractive light green with sparsely distributed white stripes. The fruits are less seeded, with 5-8 seeds per fruit compared with 25-30 seeds in a normal variety. The fruits are suitable for confectionery purpose. The yield is 200-220 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "परवल काशी अमूल्य", "label_mr": "परवर काशी अमूल्य", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "200-220 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "4979b73f-de68-447e-bfc4-38c404d9afd2", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Suphal is a pointed gourd variety released by ICAR-IIVR Varanasi and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. Its fruits stay on the plant for a long duration. The fruits are light green with mild stripes, fleshy, with soft seed. Their keeping quality is better. The fruits are suitable for culinary purpose and for sweet making. The yield is 180-200 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "परवल काशी सुफल", "label_mr": "परवर काशी सुफल", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "180-200 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "d985eaac-eecd-4cdc-8e93-ef6418fcbae3", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 202.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "pedigree method of breeding between IIHR-54 X IIHR-18 followed by selection", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Sumeet is a ridge gourd variety released by ICAR-IIHR Bengaluru. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) bred by the pedigree method from the cross IIHR-54 X IIHR-18, followed by selection. Fruits are lush green and tender, long (50-65 cm), with prominent ridges and a delicate aroma. The fruits have good transport and cooking qualities. The yield is 50 t/ha.", "label_hi": "तोरई अर्का सुमीत", "label_mr": "तुरई अर्का सुमीत", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "50 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1494b72d-8c47-4a6e-8d82-2000385a76f1", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 135, "yield_potential": 137.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "IIHR-6-1-1 x IIHR-53-1-3", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2016, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Vikram is a ridge gourd hybrid released by ICAR-IIHR Bengaluru in 2016, from the cross IIHR-6-1-1 x IIHR-53-1-3. It is early flowering; the first female flower appears in 40 days, at the 9th node from the base of the vine. The first harvest is at 46 days, and the crop duration is 120-135 days. Fruits are green, long and tender, with excellent cooking quality. They are nutritionally rich in antioxidant activity and in minerals like potassium, calcium, iron, zinc and manganese. The yield is 34.0 t/ha. It is recommended for Karnataka.", "label_hi": "तोरई अर्का विक्रम", "label_mr": "तुरई अर्का विक्रम", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "46 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Karnataka", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-135 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "34.0 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ada84a04-9fd2-4807-ab15-34e5ce5c8025", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Konkan Harita is a ridge gourd variety released in 1993 by Dr. BSKKV Dapoli (Dr. Balasaheb Sawant Konkan Krishi Vidyapeeth, Dapoli). It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV).", "label_hi": "तोरई कोंकण हरिता", "label_mr": "तुरई कोकण हरिता", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "720d3838-fa75-496c-9782-9f46df4a68a7", "maturity_days_min": 144, "maturity_days_max": 144, "yield_potential": 99.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Kiran is a ridge gourd hybrid released in 2024 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. The crop duration is 144 days. Fruits are green in colour, straight and medium in length (28 to 31 cm), and each fruit weighs 155 to 165 g. The yield is 245.68 q/ha. It is suited to the kharif and summer seasons on medium to deep, well drained soil, and is recommended for Western Maharashtra, Vidarbha and Marathwada.", "label_hi": "तोरई फुले किरण", "label_mr": "तुरई फुले किरण", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium to deep, well drained"], "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra, Vidarbha and Marathwada", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "144 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "245.68 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "96c7dd3e-c481-41c7-8cc4-132c84f2d24b", "maturity_days_min": 140, "maturity_days_max": 150, "yield_potential": 48.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Sucheta is a ridge gourd variety released in 2001 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The crop duration is 140-150 days. The foliage is dark green, and the fruits are green with prominent ridges. The yield is 120 q/ha. It is suited to the kharif and summer seasons on sandy loam soil. Under field conditions it is tolerant to downy mildew and powdery mildew diseases.", "label_hi": "तोरई फुले सुचेता", "label_mr": "तुरई फुले सुचेता", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam soil"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "140-150 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "120 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5b462b7e-a303-40f1-a10f-b30bbef413c2", "maturity_days_min": 60, "maturity_days_max": 65, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Konkan Shweta is a snake gourd variety released in 1992 by Dr. BSKKV Dapoli (Dr. Balasaheb Sawant Konkan Krishi Vidyapeeth). It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The crop duration is 60-65 days. Plants are viny with green foliage. Fruits are long, white with green discontinuous streaks at the top, and have a mild flavour. The yield is 15-20 t/ha. It is suited to the kharif and summer seasons.", "label_hi": "चिचिंडा कोंकण श्वेता", "label_mr": "पडवळ कोकण श्वेता", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "60-65 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "15-20 t/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "47260d28-8470-497e-b59d-c63d4776059b", "maturity_days_min": 190, "maturity_days_max": 190, "yield_potential": 115.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Vaibhav is a snake gourd variety released in 2001 by MPKV Rahuri under the AICRP on Vegetable Crops. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The crop duration is 190 days. The foliage is green and the stem is dark green. Fruits are white with green strips and have a smooth surface. The yield is 285 q/ha. It is suited to the kharif and summer seasons on sandy loam soil. Under field conditions it is tolerant to downy mildew disease.", "label_hi": "चिचिंडा फुले वैभव", "label_mr": "पडवळ फुले वैभव", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam soil"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "190 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "285 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "7af0f6fc-1341-4dda-80e0-b73a61ed34e3", "maturity_days_min": 140, "maturity_days_max": 150, "yield_potential": 161.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Athulya is a capsicum hybrid released by ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. The crop duration is 140-150 days. Plants are indeterminate and continuous in growth habit, with a dark green foliage cover. Fruits are firm and blocky with 3-4 lobes, of medium size, weighing 100-120 g, and are meant for the fresh green market. The yield is 35-40 t/ha. It is suitable for the kharif and rabi seasons. The hybrid has tolerance to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "शिमला मिर्च अर्का अतुल्य", "label_mr": "ढोबळी मिरची अर्का अतुल्य", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "140-150 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "35-40 t/ ha", "season_published": "kharif, rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a0793c0b-e5bd-44a0-b446-2e557275916e", "maturity_days_min": 180, "maturity_days_max": 180, "yield_potential": 60.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Improvement over IHR 225-1-1 (Var. Soroksan) followed by mass selection", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Basant is an open-pollinated capsicum variety released in 1986 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It was developed as an improvement over IHR 225-1-1 (Var. Soroksan) followed by mass selection. The crop duration is 180 days. Plants are indeterminate with yellowish green foliage. Fruits are thick fleshed, 2-3 lobed, conical and borne erect, weighing 50-80 g. They are cream coloured and turn orange red on maturity. The fruits have excellent keeping and cooking qualities. The yield is 15 t/ha. It is recommended for cultivation all over India.", "label_hi": "शिमला मिर्च अर्का बसंत", "label_mr": "ढोबळी मिरची अर्का बसंत", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "180 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "15 t/ ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "fb2241e0-8a9e-4870-8cf0-b658d026881b", "maturity_days_min": 150, "maturity_days_max": 150, "yield_potential": 64.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Improvement over IIHR-214-1 (Golden Calwonder) followed by mass selection", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Gaurav is an open-pollinated capsicum variety released in 1986 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It was developed as an improvement over IIHR-214-1 (Golden Calwonder) followed by mass selection. The crop duration is 150 days. Plants are indeterminate with green foliage. Fruits are green, blocky long, thick fleshed and 3-4 lobed, weighing 130-150 g, and are borne erect. They turn orange yellow on ripening. The yield is 16 t/ha. It is recommended for cultivation all over India. The variety is tolerant to bacterial wilt.", "label_hi": "शिमला मिर्च अर्का गौरव", "label_mr": "ढोबळी मिरची अर्का गौरव", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "150 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "16 t/ ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ce6e1560-4169-43dc-8ea8-e6d2a798c347", "maturity_days_min": 160, "maturity_days_max": 160, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Selection from Titan of USA", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Mohini is an open-pollinated capsicum variety released in 1986 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It is a selection from Titan of USA. The crop duration is 160 days. Plants are determinate with dark green foliage. Fruits are blocky, thick fleshed, 3-4 lobed and dark green, weighing 150-180 g, and hang pendent on the plant. They turn red on ripening. The fruit yield is 20 t/ha, and the seed yield in seed production is 150 kg/ha. It is recommended for cultivation all over India.", "label_hi": "शिमला मिर्च अर्का मोहिनी", "label_mr": "ढोबळी मिरची अर्का मोहिनी", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "160 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "20 t/ ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b0c9f58e-0ab8-44c5-a5fe-060dc7267779", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Yolo Wonder x HL-201", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2005, "variety_class": "hybrid", "description": "KTCPH-3 is a capsicum hybrid released in 2005 by the ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI) Regional Station at Katrain. It was bred by crossing Yolo Wonder with HL-201, so its parentage is Yolo Wonder x HL-201. The All India Coordinated Research Project on Vegetable Crops (AICRP-VC) has recommended this hybrid for cultivation in its zones I, VI and VII. Capsicum growers in these three zones can choose it for their fields.", "label_hi": "शिमला मिर्च KTCPH-3", "label_mr": "ढोबळी मिरची KTCPH-3", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "AICRP-VC recommended zones I, VI, VII", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "48fa228a-c94a-41b2-8d72-52db99ecec03", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 91.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "hybrid between Yolo Wonder and Runion Yellow (code Kt-1)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": "hybrid", "description": "Pusa Deepti is a capsicum hybrid released by ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It is a hybrid between Yolo Wonder and Runion Yellow (code Kt-1). It is very early, and the first harvest is ready in 60-70 days. Plants are erect, medium and bushy. Fruits are conical, 9-11 cm long and yellowish green, turning dark red at maturity. The yield is 225 q/ha. It is recommended for cultivation all over India. The hybrid is tolerant to bacterial leaf spot and anthracnose.", "label_hi": "शिमला मिर्च पूसा दीप्ति", "label_mr": "ढोबळी मिरची पूसा दीप्ती", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "60-70 days", "recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "225 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "dc96d860-2932-45c1-96fa-907dd6da626c", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 70, "yield_potential": 48.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi"], "parentage": "mass selection from IIHR Acc. No. 19528", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Isha is an open-pollinated coriander variety released by ICAR-Indian Institute of Horticultural Research (IIHR), Bengaluru. It was developed by mass selection from IIHR Acc. No. 19528. It is a multi-cut type with bushy plants and broad leaves. The first cutting is taken 40 days after sowing, and further cuttings follow at 15-day intervals, giving 3 cuttings in all. Days to harvest are 70. Flowering is late, at 50 days after sowing. The leaves have good aroma, keep for 21 days under refrigeration and contain 167 mg vitamin C per 100 g fresh weight. The yield is 12 t/ha. It is suitable for the kharif and rabi seasons.", "label_hi": "धनिया (पत्ती) अर्का ईशा", "label_mr": "कोथिंबीर अर्का ईशा", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "40 days", "season": "kharif", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "12 t/ha", "season_published": "kharif, rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "51c5d357-9a5f-44c9-81aa-7992081585fb", "maturity_days_min": 35, "maturity_days_max": 50, "yield_potential": 42.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": ["rabi", "summer"], "parentage": "DPL-COR-1; selection from various local genotypes at CES Wakavali", "notification_number": "4272(E)", "notification_date": "2019-11-26", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Konkan Kasturi (DPL-COR-1) is an open-pollinated coriander variety released in 2013 by Dr. Balasaheb Sawant Konkan Krishi Vidyapeeth (DBSKKV), Dapoli. It was developed by selection from various local genotypes at CES Wakavali and was notified vide S.O. 4272(E) dated 26 November 2019. The crop duration is 35-50 days. Plants are of spreading type, up to 35 cm tall, with broad leaves, an average of 39 leaves per plant and 6 to 7 branches. It is suitable for the green leaves purpose and has a high leaf to shoot ratio. It has high aroma and good shelf life. The yield is 106 q/ha. It suits the rabi and summer seasons and is recommended for the Konkan region of Maharashtra.", "label_hi": "धनिया (पत्ती) कोंकण कस्तूरी", "label_mr": "कोथिंबीर कोकण कस्तुरी", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "recommended_areas_published": "konkan region of Maharashtra (India)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "35-50 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "106 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "0b1de1ac-d65d-4c3c-bc56-b7e3e36df5b4", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 184.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Punjab Khushboo is a coriander variety that was released by Punjab Agricultural University (PAU), Ludhiana. The plants have a semi-erect habit and branch out profusely. The variety does not bolt early. In all, it gives five harvests of green foliage. The leaves of this variety are medium-broad, green and tender, and they have an excellent aroma. The yield of this variety is 184 q/acre.", "label_hi": "धनिया (पत्ती) पंजाब खुशबू", "label_mr": "कोथिंबीर पंजाब खुशबू", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "184 quintal per acre", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "86a50d3e-91a9-4034-aec3-23e2dffad72e", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Early Bunching is a fenugreek (methi) variety released by ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It is meant for leafy use and is suitable for multiple harvesting, so the leaves can be cut more than once from the same crop. The variety is rich in dietary minerals. It is resistant to downy mildew. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh, where it is listed among the improved fenugreek varieties.", "label_hi": "मेथी पूसा अर्ली बंचिंग", "label_mr": "मेथी पूसा अर्ली बंचिंग", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh (listed among improved fenugreek varieties for Uttar Pradesh)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "cd46a21a-5cbc-4589-9b01-360b7c3a09d9", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 52.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Agrifound White (G-41) is a clonal garlic variety released by NHRDF, Nashik. The bulbs are compact and silvery white with creamy flesh, and measure 3.5 to 4.5 cm in diameter. Each bulb has 20-25 cloves, which are bigger and elongated. The bulbs are good for storage. Total soluble solids are 41%, dry matter is 42.78% and pyruvic acid is 27 micro mole/g. The yield is 130 q/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh. The variety is susceptible to purple blotch and stemphylium blight.", "label_hi": "लहसुन एग्रीफाउंड व्हाइट (G-41)", "label_mr": "लसूण ॲग्रीफाउंड व्हाईट (G-41)", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "130 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5978d41d-580f-4de7-9295-3a7a0e7604f6", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 135, "yield_potential": 48.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Bhima Omkar is a clonal garlic variety released by ICAR-Directorate of Onion and Garlic Research (DOGR), Rajgurunagar, Pune. It matures in 120-135 days. Plants are semi-erect and 50-60 cm tall, with 10-12 dark green, slightly concave leaves 0.9-1.1 cm wide. The pseudo-stem is 6-8 cm long and 0.6-0.8 cm wide. It is a soft-neck tropical type, suitable for braiding. Bulbs are white and compact, circular in longitudinal section and elliptical in cross section, 3.0-3.5 cm in diameter, with 18-20 cloves. Cloves are white with whitish flesh and 0.8-1.2 cm in diameter. Bulbs store for 6-8 months. Total soluble solids are 32.2 °Brix, and allicin is 2.7 mg/g on fresh weight basis and 7.8 mg/g on dry weight basis. The yield is 10-12 t/ha. In rabi it is recommended for Delhi, Gujarat, Haryana and Rajasthan. It is moderately tolerant to thrips.", "label_hi": "लहसुन भीमा ओंकार", "label_mr": "लसूण भीमा ओंकार", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "recommended_areas_published": "For Rabi: Delhi, Gujarat, Haryana and Rajasthan", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-135 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "10-12 t/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "c385f241-6acd-4071-ac5e-d81ed366864e", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 32.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Bhima Purple is a clonal garlic variety released by ICAR-Directorate of Onion and Garlic Research (DOGR), Rajgurunagar, Pune. Plants are semi-erect and 40-45 cm tall, with 11-12 medium green, slightly concave leaves 0.9-1.2 cm wide. The pseudo-stem is 5-7 cm long. It is a soft-neck tropical type, suitable for braiding. Bulbs are purple and compact, ovate in longitudinal section and circular in cross section, 2.4-2.8 cm in diameter, with 16-20 cloves. Cloves are purple with whitish flesh and 1.0-1.2 cm in diameter. Bulbs store for 6-8 months. Total soluble solids are 33.6 °Brix, and allicin is 2.9 mg/g on fresh weight basis and 9.6 mg/g on dry weight basis. The yield is 6-8 t/ha. In rabi it is recommended for Andhra Pradesh, Bihar, Delhi, Haryana, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Punjab and Uttar Pradesh. It is field tolerant to thrips.", "label_hi": "लहसुन भीमा पर्पल", "label_mr": "लसूण भीमा पर्पल", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "recommended_areas_published": "For Rabi: Andhra Pradesh, Bihar, Delhi, Haryana, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Punjab and Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "6-8 t/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2ec3c056-0c98-42d9-9724-515b7f2cbdd4", "maturity_days_min": 130, "maturity_days_max": 140, "yield_potential": 60.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Godavari is a clonal garlic variety released in 1987 by the All India Coordinated Research Project (AICRP) on Vegetable Crops at Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. The crop duration is 130-140 days. Bulbs are of medium size, with 25-30 cloves per bulb, and the cloves are pink in colour. The yield is 150 q/ha. It is a rabi season variety and suits medium black, well-drained soil. The variety is tolerant to mites.", "label_hi": "लहसुन गोदावरी", "label_mr": "लसूण गोदावरी", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "soil_types": ["Medium black, well drained"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "130-140 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "150 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "23c74e12-b62f-411c-82f0-35cbe4c80874", "maturity_days_min": 135, "maturity_days_max": 150, "yield_potential": 62.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Baswant is a clonal garlic variety released in 2007 by the Onion and Grape Research Station of Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV) at Pimpalgaon Baswant, Nashik. The crop duration is 135-150 days. Bulbs are violet and medium to big in size, with a bulb weight of 25.11 g. Cloves are big, weighing 0.97 g, and are pink and attractive. It has higher pungency and a sulphur content of 46.14 mg/100 g. The yield is 154 q/ha. It is a rabi season variety and suits medium black, well-drained soil. The variety is moderately resistant to purple blotch and stemphylium blight.", "label_hi": "लहसुन फुले बसवंत", "label_mr": "लसूण फुले बसवंत", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "soil_types": ["Medium black, well drained"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "135-150 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "154 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "7631b5c4-f0b6-4c16-9f83-7de2ea69d18d", "maturity_days_min": 140, "maturity_days_max": 150, "yield_potential": 66.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Nilima is a clonal garlic variety released in 2014 by the All India Coordinated Research Project (AICRP) on Vegetable Crops at Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. The crop duration is 140-150 days. It produces attractive violet coloured bulbs of big size. The yield is 160-165 q/ha. It is a rabi season variety and suits medium black, well-drained soil. The variety is moderately resistant to purple blotch disease and to thrips and mites.", "label_hi": "लहसुन फुले नीलिमा", "label_mr": "लसूण फुले नीलिमा", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "soil_types": ["Medium black, well drained"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "140-150 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "160-165 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ded69060-5d42-40e9-bd5c-61e14d77867e", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Yamuna Safed-3 (G-282) is a clonal garlic variety released by NHRDF, Nashik. The bulbs are creamy white and bigger sized, 4.5-6 cm in diameter, with 15-16 cloves per bulb. Clove diameter is 1.2-1.5 cm. The bulbs have medium storage quality. Total soluble solids are 38-42%, dry matter is 39-43% and pyruvic acid is 25 micro mole/g. It is suitable for export. The yield is 175-200 q/ha. It is recommended for Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Haryana, Gujarat, Punjab, Rajasthan, Uttar Pradesh and Chhattisgarh.", "label_hi": "लहसुन यमुना सफेद-3 (G-282)", "label_mr": "लसूण यमुना सफेद-3 (G-282)", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Haryana, Gujarat, Punjab, Rajasthan, Uttar Pradesh and Chhattisgarh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "175-200 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3bbb09a1-8cd0-4365-b1b1-b9cc21baa62f", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 125.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Ooty 1 is a beetroot variety that was released by Tamil Nadu Agricultural University (TNAU), Coimbatore. It is an open-pollinated variety, also called an OPV. The roots of this variety are blood red in colour, and the skin of the root is thin. The yield of this variety is 31 t/ha. Ooty 1 is recommended for cultivation in the state of Tamil Nadu.", "label_hi": "चुकंदर ऊटी 1", "label_mr": "बीट ऊटी 1", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Tamil Nadu", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "31 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "8299fe88-eff3-430c-b1f0-059d7500a9d7", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Mass selection", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1993, "variety_class": null, "description": "Hisar Gairic is a carrot variety released by CCS HAU, Hisar in 1993. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed by mass selection. The roots are light brick-red in colour with a self-coloured core, and they are longer than the roots of Pusa Kesar. The roots are high in carotene. The yield of this variety is 300 q/ha. It is recommended for cultivation in Haryana.", "label_hi": "गाजर हिसार गैरिक", "label_mr": "गाजर हिसार गैरिक", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Haryana", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "300 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3eb381d4-487c-4329-a304-3323b0f2167a", "maturity_days_min": 85, "maturity_days_max": 95, "yield_potential": 141.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Selection", "notification_number": "3254", "notification_date": "2022-07-20", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Arun is a carrot variety released by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi in 2022 and notified under S.O. 3254 dated 2022-07-20. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed by selection. The roots are ready for harvest in 85-95 days. They are attractive red in colour, Danvers (triangular) in shape, 21-23 cm long and 110-125 g in weight, with a self-coloured core. The TSS (total soluble solids) of the roots is 8.5-9.0 °B. The yield is 300-350 q/ha. It is recommended for Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Goa, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Puducherry.", "label_hi": "गाजर काशी अरुण", "label_mr": "गाजर काशी अरुण", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Goa, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Puducherry", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "85-95 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "300-350 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3522a2f3-c5c4-434a-a4bb-4817e2854675", "maturity_days_min": 95, "maturity_days_max": 105, "yield_potential": 89.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Krishna is a carrot variety released by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi in 2019 and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The roots are ready for harvest in 95-105 days, and the plants are tolerant to bolting. The roots are black (solid purple) in colour and Danvers (triangular) in shape, with a self-coloured core and fewer secondary roots and scars. The anthocyanin content is 285 mg/100g FW (fresh weight), and the roots are a rich source of phenolics and antioxidants. They are used for salad, juice, halwa, kanji (fermented juice) and nutraceutical purposes. The yield is 20-22 t/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "गाजर काशी कृष्णा", "label_mr": "गाजर काशी कृष्णा", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "95-105 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "20-22 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "7369b88b-a7be-4922-9cd6-f9e02f9b8340", "maturity_days_min": 80, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 121.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Selection from Local Red × Nantes Half Long", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1963, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Kesar is a carrot variety released by ICAR-IARI, New Delhi in 1963. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) selected from the cross Local Red × Nantes Half Long. It matures in 80-90 days. The plants have short tops. The roots are tapering and deep red in colour, with a small, self-coloured core. The roots are rich in carotene. The yield is 300 q/ha. The variety can tolerate heat. It is recommended for cultivation all over India.", "label_hi": "गाजर पूसा केसर", "label_mr": "गाजर पूसा केसर", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "All over India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "80-90 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "300 q/ha", "season_published": "sowing August - early October (as stated; no season name given)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a90ed3e4-40f4-4d2b-a227-9bc249fc8b1a", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 113.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pusa Kesar × Nantes", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1994, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Meghali is a carrot variety released by ICAR-IARI, New Delhi in 1994. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed from the cross Pusa Kesar × Nantes. The roots are ready for harvest in 110-120 days. The plants have short tops. The roots are smooth and stumpy to slightly tapering in shape, with orange flesh and a self-coloured core. The yield is 250-280 q/ha. It is recommended for Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra.", "label_hi": "गाजर पूसा मेघाली", "label_mr": "गाजर पूसा मेघाली", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-120 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "250-280 q/ha", "season_published": "early sowing (August-September), late sowing (October-November)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3b842627-18aa-4caf-811b-b89bca29b1e3", "maturity_days_min": 85, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 133.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2008, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Rudhira is a carrot variety released by ICAR-IARI, New Delhi in 2008. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) of the tropical type. It matures in 85-90 days, and the roots are ready for harvest during the middle of December. Bolting is delayed in this variety. The roots are long, red and obtriangular in shape, with a self-coloured core. The carotenoid content is 7.41 mg per 100 g, and the TSS (total soluble solids) is 9.5 °Brix. The yield is 330 q/ha. It is recommended for Delhi and the NCR (National Capital Region).", "label_hi": "गाजर पूसा रुधिरा", "label_mr": "गाजर पूसा रुधिरा", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "NCR (DAC checklist); Delhi and NCR (Indian J. Hort. 2018)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "85-90 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "330 q/ha", "season_published": "sowing mid September to October (as stated; no season name given)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2f7afdbf-f767-414c-b2f3-122bff351f02", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 75, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi"], "parentage": "(Arka Bold x Arka Komal) 99-17-2-1-4-12-3, pedigree method", "notification_number": "456(E)", "notification_date": "2012-03-06", "release_year": 2012, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Anoop is a French bean variety released by ICAR-IIHR, Bengaluru in 2012 and notified under S.O. 456(E) dated 2012-03-06. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed by the pedigree method from line 99-17-2-1-4-12-3 of the cross (Arka Bold x Arka Komal). The crop duration is 70-75 days. The plants are bushy and photo-insensitive. The pods are flat, straight and 17-18 cm long. The yield is 20 t/ha. It is suited to the kharif and rabi seasons and is recommended for all over India, including Karnataka. It is resistant to rust and bacterial blight.", "label_hi": "फ्रेंच बीन अर्का अनूप", "label_mr": "फरसबी अर्का अनूप", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "All over India (DAC checklist); Karnataka (IIHR notified list)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70-75 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "20 t/ha", "season_published": "kharif, rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "d057ef0b-b18b-422b-992d-c9c292536743", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 75, "yield_potential": 80.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Sel.9 (designation as printed; origin of the selection not stated)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Komal is a French bean variety released by ICAR-IIHR, Bengaluru. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) from the selection Sel.9. The crop duration is 70-75 days. The plants are erect, bushy and photo-insensitive, with bright green stem and foliage. The pods are slender, long and green. The yield is 20 t/ha, and the seed yield is 1500 kg/ha. It is good for transportation and has excellent cooking quality. It is recommended for Himachal Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir, the hills of Uttar Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala. It is susceptible to rust.", "label_hi": "फ्रेंच बीन अर्का कोमल", "label_mr": "फरसबी अर्का कोमल", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "H.P., J&K, Hills of U.P., M.P., Maharashtra, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Kerala", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70-75 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "20 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "02c36af1-0753-40c2-a5ef-0584ae19a419", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 68.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "1480(E)", "notification_date": "2021-04-01", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Baingani is a French bean variety released by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi in 2021 and notified under S.O. 1480(E) dated 2021-04-01. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) with a pole growth habit. Flowering takes 70-80 days. The pods are purple in colour, 14-15 cm long, round, slightly curved and fleshy, with a smooth surface, and they are free from parchment. The seeds are light brown. The anthocyanin content is 7.0-7.25 mg/100 g FW (fresh weight). The yield is 150-170 q/ha. It is recommended for Jammu & Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Goa, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Puducherry.", "label_hi": "फ्रेंच बीन काशी बैंगनी", "label_mr": "फरसबी काशी बैंगनी", "aes": {"flowering_days": "70-80 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Jammu & Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh, Uttarakhand, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Goa, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Puducherry", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "150-170 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "136e9b80-a314-401e-bbf9-a40efd298a72", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Rajhans is a French bean variety released by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi in 2019 and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) with a bushy growth habit. The pods are dark green, thin, round, slightly curved and fleshy, with a smooth surface, and they are free from parchment. Seed development in the pods is slower. The seeds are white. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh. It is tolerant to golden yellow mosaic virus.", "label_hi": "फ्रेंच बीन काशी राजहंस", "label_mr": "फरसबी काशी राजहंस", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5fc8dbb3-ac8b-44a8-b714-38ba3f2a37a7", "maturity_days_min": 90, "maturity_days_max": 100, "yield_potential": 60.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Surekha is a French bean variety released by MPKV (NARP Ganeshkhind, Pune) in 1997. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The crop duration is 90-100 days. The pods are flat, light green in colour and 9-10 cm long. The yield is 150 q/ha. It is suited to the kharif season. It is recommended for Western Maharashtra, on light to medium, well-drained soils.", "label_hi": "फ्रेंच बीन फुले सुरेखा", "label_mr": "फरसबी फुले सुरेखा", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Light to medium and well drained"], "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "90-100 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "150 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "bee8dad9-af39-4bcc-803f-4547d1948302", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 80, "yield_potential": 68.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Suyash is a French bean variety released by MPKV (NARP Ganeshkhind, Pune) in 2003. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The crop duration is 70-80 days. The pods are attractive, tender, smooth and green, and straight to slightly curved. The yield is 160-170 q/ha. It is suited to the kharif and rabi seasons. It is recommended for Maharashtra, including Western Maharashtra, on light to medium, well-drained soils.", "label_hi": "फ्रेंच बीन फुले सुयश", "label_mr": "फरसबी फुले सुयश", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Light to medium and well drained"], "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra (MPKV); Maharashtra (DAC checklist)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70-80 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "160-170 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "87dddb93-d28b-417b-ae85-87c70f7a0cc1", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 202.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "1480(E)", "notification_date": "2021-04-01", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Aardra is a radish variety released by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi in 2021 and notified under S.O. 1480(E) dated 2021-04-01. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The leaves are dark green and soft, with entire (uncut) leaf margins. A temperature of 12-25°C is suitable for its growth and root development. The roots are white and keep their white colour (retentive white); they are long, tapered or icicle-shaped and 22-24 cm long. The yield is 45-50 t/ha. It is recommended for West Bengal and Assam.", "label_hi": "मूली काशी आर्द्रा", "label_mr": "मुळा काशी आर्द्रा", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "West Bengal, Assam", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "45-50 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a2b0b0fe-b27f-4ee7-a184-6f153d5a0949", "maturity_days_min": 40, "maturity_days_max": 42, "yield_potential": 182.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "simple recurrent selection (at ICAR-IIVR)", "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Lohit is a radish variety released by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi in 2019 and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV) developed by simple recurrent selection at ICAR-IIVR. The roots are ready for harvest in 40-42 days. They are attractive red, icicle-shaped and 22-23 cm long, and are tolerant to pithiness. The roots are used for salad dressing. Their antioxidant content is 80-100 % higher than white radish, their anthocyanin content is 4 mg/100g FW (fresh weight), and they are a good source of vitamin C. The yield is 40-45.0 t/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh.", "label_hi": "मूली काशी लोहित", "label_mr": "मुळा काशी लोहित", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "40-42 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "40-45.0 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2c681d06-5997-41cd-9e1e-856654587b04", "maturity_days_min": 45, "maturity_days_max": 50, "yield_potential": 141.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "692(E)", "notification_date": "2019-02-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Mooli 40 is a radish variety released by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi in 2019 and notified under S.O. 692(E) dated 2019-02-05. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The roots are ready for harvest in 45-50 days. Bolting is delayed, and the temperature for root development is 15-40 °C. The roots are attractive white and icicle-shaped, and are tolerant to pithiness. The yield is 30-35 t/ha. It is suited to the summer season and is recommended for Uttar Pradesh. It is tolerant to heat.", "label_hi": "मूली काशी मूली 40", "label_mr": "मुळा काशी मूली 40", "aes": {"season": "summer", "recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "45-50 days (days to harvest)", "yield_published": "30-35 t/ha", "season_published": "summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "07ed20a3-e31e-44fe-a506-72e64221c616", "maturity_days_min": 115, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 7.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2020, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPF 16-13 (Harit) is a field pea variety released in 2020 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. The crop duration is 115-120 days. The plants are tall and leafy. The seeds are green in colour and round in shape. The yield is 1752 kg/ha. It is recommended for the North Eastern Plain Zone, which covers Bihar, Assam, Chhattisgarh, West Bengal and the eastern part of Uttar Pradesh. It is resistant to powdery mildew and moderately tolerant to rust.", "label_hi": "मटर (दलहनी) IPF 16-13 (हरित)", "label_mr": "वाटाणा (कडधान्य) IPF 16-13 (हरित)", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "North Eastern Plain Zone comprised of Bihar, Assam, Chhattisgarh, West Bengal and eastern part of Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "115-120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "1752 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "091e4050-62c5-46c9-87e9-67187cfe4134", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 130, "yield_potential": 10.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPFD 12-8 (Aakash) is a field pea variety released in 2020 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. The crop duration is 120-130 days. The plants are dwarf and leafy. The seeds are medium in size, round, smooth and creamish white, and the cotyledons are yellow. The yield is 25 q/ha. It is recommended for the whole of Uttar Pradesh. It is resistant to both powdery mildew and rust.", "label_hi": "मटर (दलहनी) IPFD 12-8 (आकाश)", "label_mr": "वाटाणा (कडधान्य) IPFD 12-8 (आकाश)", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "whole Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-130 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "25 qt/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "bce3b757-1a30-4568-81cd-42cbfe0bcea9", "maturity_days_min": 102, "maturity_days_max": 102, "yield_potential": 9.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPFD 2014-2 is a field pea variety from ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. It matures in 102 days. The plants are dwarf and fall in the dwarf category. The seeds are bold, with a mottled violet-tan colour. The yield is 2270 kg/ha. It is recommended for the central zone, which covers Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Maharashtra and parts of Rajasthan. It is resistant to powdery mildew and moderately resistant to Ascochyta blight. It is also moderately resistant to pod borer, aphid and leaf miner.", "label_hi": "मटर (दलहनी) IPFD 2014-2", "label_mr": "वाटाणा (कडधान्य) IPFD 2014-2", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "central zone comprised of Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Maharashtra and parts of Rajasthan", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "102 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "2270 Kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "44d675af-1a95-4176-8908-57fc9c911c61", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 10.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pant Pea 243 is a field pea variety. It was released in 2018 by G.B. Pant University of Agriculture & Technology, Pantnagar, under AICRP-MULLaRP. The plants belong to the tall category. This variety is grown in the rabi season. Its yield is 20-25 q/ha. It is recommended for the Central Zone of India, which includes the states of Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh and also parts of Rajasthan.", "label_hi": "मटर (दलहनी) पंत पी 243", "label_mr": "वाटाणा (कडधान्य) पंत पी 243", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone of India (Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh and Parts of Rajasthan)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "20-25 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5008b41d-7af7-4dd2-b794-7f4d4ae6d9c9", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 9.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pant Pea 484 is an open-pollinated (OPV) field pea variety released in 2024 by ICAR-AICRP on Pulses, G.B. Pant University of Agriculture and Technology, Pantnagar, Uttarakhand. It matures in 120 days. Its protein content is 26.17%. The yield is 23.33 q/ha. It is a rabi season variety and suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is recommended for Punjab, Haryana, Delhi, North-West and Central Rajasthan, Western Uttar Pradesh, the plains of Uttarakhand, and Jammu and Kashmir. It is resistant to Ascochyta blight and moderately resistant to rust and powdery mildew. It is also moderately resistant to aphid and pod borer.", "label_hi": "मटर (दलहनी) पंत पी 484", "label_mr": "वाटाणा (कडधान्य) पंत पी 484", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "protein_content": "26.17%", "recommended_areas_published": "Punjab, Haryana, Delhi, North-West & Central Rajasthan, Western Uttar Pradesh, Plains of Uttarakhand and Jammu and Kashmir", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "23.33 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "7d3f655c-c3fe-453a-b13c-ab7ebc0d6ca1", "maturity_days_min": 80, "maturity_days_max": 82, "yield_potential": 6.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Viraj (GRB-701) is a rajma (kidney bean) variety released in 2022 by NARP, Ganeshkhind, Pune (MPKV). The crop duration is 80-82 days. The seed coat is dough-white with purple streaks. The seeds are bold, with a 100-seed weight of 35.80 g. The protein content is 24.26% and the carbohydrate content is 64.72%. The yield is 16-17 q/ha. It suits the kharif and rabi seasons and is recommended for the kharif season in Western Maharashtra. It suits well-drained, medium to deep soil. It is tolerant to Fusarium wilt and bean common mosaic virus (BCMV).", "label_hi": "राजमा फुले विराज (GRB-701)", "label_mr": "राजमा फुले विराज (GRB-701)", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Well drained, Medium to deep"], "protein_content": "24.26 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Kharif season in Western Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "80-82 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "16-17 q ha-1", "season_published": "kharif, rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "65850e27-58e8-481f-bc83-8f3efbeefc72", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 125, "yield_potential": 5.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "three way cross (DPL 44 × DPL 62) × DPL 58", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPL 225 is a lentil variety from ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. It was developed from a three-way cross, (DPL 44 × DPL 62) × DPL 58. It matures in 120-125 days. The seeds are small, with a 100-seed weight of 2.1 g. The seed coat is brown with dots, and the cotyledons are red. The yield is 12-14 q/ha. It is recommended for the entire state of Uttar Pradesh. It is resistant to rust and Fusarium wilt.", "label_hi": "मसूर IPL 225", "label_mr": "मसूर IPL 225", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "entire Uttar Pradesh state", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-125 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "12-14 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "13d8ad62-e493-42f5-8621-7a315cf51301", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 114, "yield_potential": 6.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPL 534 is a lentil variety released in 2019 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. It is early maturing and is ready in 110-114 days. The seeds are brown and large, with a 100-seed weight of 3.2 g, and the cotyledons are red. The yield is 14-16 q/ha. It is recommended for the entire state of Madhya Pradesh. It is resistant to three diseases: rust, Fusarium wilt and Stemphylium blight.", "label_hi": "मसूर IPL 534", "label_mr": "मसूर IPL 534", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "entire Madhya Pradesh state", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-114 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "14-16 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ae4718b6-6ccc-465a-9aa1-d6455b60f7bd", "maturity_days_min": 130, "maturity_days_max": 135, "yield_potential": 7.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "DPL 59 x IPL 105", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pant L 8 is a lentil variety released in 2010 by G.B. Pant University of Agriculture & Technology, Pantnagar, under AICRP-MULLaRP. It was developed from the cross DPL 59 × IPL 105. It matures in 130-135 days. The seeds are small. The yield is 15-18 q/ha. It is recommended for the North Western Plain Zone (NWPZ). It is moderately resistant to both rust and Fusarium wilt.", "label_hi": "मसूर पंत L 8", "label_mr": "मसूर पंत L 8", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "North Western Plain Zone (NWPZ)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "130-135 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "15-18 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a440c982-8498-4fbb-a9a8-111a55a160d0", "maturity_days_min": 128, "maturity_days_max": 128, "yield_potential": 6.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pant Lentil 14 (PL 320) is an open-pollinated (OPV) lentil variety released in 2024 by ICAR-AICRP on Pulses, G.B. Pant University of Agriculture and Technology, Pantnagar, Uttarakhand. It matures in 128 days. The seed protein content is 25.72%. The yield is 15.55 q/ha. It is a rabi season variety and suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is recommended for Punjab, Haryana, Delhi, North-West and Central Rajasthan, Western Uttar Pradesh, the plains of Uttarakhand, and Jammu and Kashmir. It is resistant to rust and Stemphylium blight, and moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt and Ascochyta blight. It is also moderately resistant to pod borer and aphid.", "label_hi": "मसूर पंत लेंटिल 14 (PL 320)", "label_mr": "मसूर पंत लेंटिल 14 (PL 320)", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "protein_content": "25.72%", "recommended_areas_published": "Punjab, Haryana, Delhi, North-West & Central Rajasthan, Western Uttar Pradesh, Plains of Uttarakhand and Jammu and Kashmir", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "128 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "15.55 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "da415afe-52ed-4f9f-a3ab-c7ac8a8beebb", "maturity_days_min": 90, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 40.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pedigree selection from F6 generation of (Bonneville X IIHR 209) X Freezer 656", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Arka Ajit is an open-pollinated (OPV) pea variety from ICAR-IIHR, Bengaluru. It was developed by pedigree selection from the F6 generation of the cross (Bonneville × IIHR 209) × Freezer 656. It is a mid-season variety with a crop duration of 90 days. The pods are medium long and light green. The seeds are bold, green and sweet. The yield is 10.0 t/ha. It is resistant to both powdery mildew and rust.", "label_hi": "मटर अर्का अजित", "label_mr": "वाटाणा अर्का अजित", "aes": {"source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "90 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10.0 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3057b0c2-c3fe-4759-8af5-119e2a519494", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 48.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "2277(E)", "notification_date": "2015-08-17", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Ageti is an open-pollinated (OPV) pea variety released in 2015 by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi, and notified on 17 August 2015. It is an early variety with determinate growth and dark green foliage. Each plant bears 8-9 pods, and each pod weighs 9-10 g. The shelling percentage is 48.5-50%. The yield is 100-120 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and Punjab.", "label_hi": "मटर काशी अगेती", "label_mr": "वाटाणा काशी अगेती", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and Punjab", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "100-120 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1f684065-e8ca-4457-9634-fcba4b56e301", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 48.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "597(E)", "notification_date": "2006-04-25", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Nandini is an open-pollinated (OPV) pea variety released in 2006 by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi, and notified on 25 April 2006. It is an early variety. Each plant bears 7-8 pods. The pods are 8-9 cm long and hold 8-9 seeds each. The shelling percentage is 47-48%. The yield is 110-120 q/ha. It is recommended for Himachal Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir, Uttarakhand, Bihar, Jharkhand, Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Karnataka, Kerala, Puducherry and Tamil Nadu.", "label_hi": "मटर काशी नंदिनी", "label_mr": "वाटाणा काशी नंदिनी", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Himachal Pradesh, Jammu & Kashmir, Uttarakhand, Bihar, Jharkhand, Punjab, Uttar Pradesh, Karnataka, Kerala, Puducherry and Tamil Nadu", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "110-120 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "93c760c5-59a0-4a5b-91a6-93c55e8f5636", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 56.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "2363(E)", "notification_date": "2012-10-04", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kashi Samridhi is an open-pollinated (OPV) pea variety released in 2012 by ICAR-IIVR, Varanasi, and notified on 4 October 2012. It is a semi-determinate, late-maturing type, and the first harvest is at 90-95 days. Each plant bears 13-14 pods. The pods are dark green, straight and slightly curved at the tips, 7.5-8.0 cm long, with an average weight of 5-6 g and 7-8 seeds per pod. The shelling percentage is 46-48%. It is sweet, with a total sugar content of 3.86%. The yield is 120-140 q/ha. It is recommended for Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Bihar and Jharkhand. It is resistant to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "मटर काशी समृद्धि", "label_mr": "वाटाणा काशी समृद्धी", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "90-95 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Bihar and Jharkhand", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "120-140 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b352b5fb-84c8-4813-983b-87802768f339", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 110, "yield_potential": 42.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Priya is an open-pollinated (OPV) pea variety released in 2010 by AICRP on Vegetable Crops, MPKV, Rahuri. The crop duration is 100-110 days. The pods are straight, green, tender and sweet, with 8-10 grains in each pod. The yield is 100-105 q/ha. This variety is grown in the rabi season and is suited to sandy loam soil. It is tolerant to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "मटर फुले प्रिया", "label_mr": "वाटाणा फुले प्रिया", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "soil_types": ["Sandy loam soil"], "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100-110 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "100-105 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "0be6c8dd-e9e9-404e-a6da-baeb44c5e86a", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 20.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Shree is an open-pollinated (OPV) pea variety from ICAR-IARI, New Delhi. It is an early variety, and the first harvest is ready at 50-55 days. The pods are dark green and hold 6-7 seeds each. The yield is 4.5-5.0 t/ha. It is recommended by AICRP Vegetable Crops for Jammu & Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh and Uttarakhand. It is resistant to Fusarium wilt and tolerant to heat.", "label_hi": "मटर पूसा श्री", "label_mr": "वाटाणा पूसा श्री", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "50-55 days", "recommended_areas_published": "Jammu & Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh and Uttarakhand (recommended by AICRP Vegetable Crops)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "4.5-5.0 t/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "17daaf6b-11ec-409c-a3bf-05c1b2ef44e0", "maturity_days_min": 115, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 8.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "3220(E)", "notification_date": "2019-09-06", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPC 2006-77 was released in 2019 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur, and notified vide S.O. 3220(E) dated 2019-09-06. It is an open-pollinated (OPV) desi chickpea that matures in 115-120 days. The seeds are light brown and medium in size, with a 100-seed weight of 16.5 g. Seed protein content is more than 24%. Yield is 20-22 q/ha. It is recommended for late-sown, irrigated conditions in the Central Zone. The variety is resistant to Fusarium wilt and moderately resistant to dry root rot, stunt and collar rot.", "label_hi": "चना IPC 2006-77", "label_mr": "हरभरा IPC 2006-77", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "irrigated", "protein_content": ">24%", "recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone, late sown condition", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "115-120 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "20-22 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "fe8ba177-f8e6-4312-bfec-6686fe652e2d", "maturity_days_min": 105, "maturity_days_max": 110, "yield_potential": 13.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": 13.0, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Selection from local germplasm", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Kripa was released in 2009 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. It is an open-pollinated (OPV) variety developed by selection from local germplasm. The crop duration is 105-110 days. It is an extra-large seeded kabuli type with milky white seeds and a 100-seed weight of 59.4 g, and it fetches a premium market price. Under irrigated conditions it yields 30-32 q/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh and Karnataka, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm.", "label_hi": "चना कृपा", "label_mr": "हरभरा कृपा", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "irrigated", "soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Karnataka", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "105-110 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "30-32 q/ha (irrigated)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1707d154-0941-4f90-80c7-64a01fee2eeb", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 115, "yield_potential": 5.3, "yield_rainfed": 5.3, "yield_irrigated": 12.1, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule G 12 was released in 1989 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. The crop duration is 110-115 days. The seeds are an attractive yellowish brown colour and medium in size. Under rainfed conditions it yields 12-13 q/ha. The variety can be grown under both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is recommended for Maharashtra, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm.", "label_hi": "चना फुले G 12", "label_mr": "हरभरा फुले G 12", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-115 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "12-13 q/ha (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "4bcb7e5f-332b-4710-bacc-584d320b6edf", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 115, "yield_potential": 4.9, "yield_rainfed": 4.9, "yield_irrigated": 13.0, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Virat was released in 2001 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. It is an open-pollinated (OPV) variety with a crop duration of 110-115 days. It is an extra bold seeded kabuli type and fetches a higher market price. Under rainfed conditions it yields 10-12 q/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm. The variety is resistant to Fusarium wilt.", "label_hi": "चना विराट", "label_mr": "हरभरा विराट", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-115 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10-12 q/ha (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b7bc278f-43b7-4ea7-bc4b-38fd2fcf8b8a", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 105, "yield_potential": 2.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Man is a horse gram (kulthi) variety released in 1986 by AICRP on DLA, Solapur, MPKV, Rahuri. The plants are of erect type, and the crop duration is 100-105 days. The grain is ash in colour. In terms of quality, the grain contains 18.37% crude protein and 36.23 mg/100g iron. The yield is 6-7 q/ha. This variety is recommended for cultivation on light soils in Maharashtra state.", "label_hi": "कुलथी मान", "label_mr": "कुळीथ मान", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Light soil"], "protein_content": "18.37%", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra state", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100-105 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "6-7 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2bbabb8d-0109-490f-a966-0873660859b7", "maturity_days_min": 90, "maturity_days_max": 95, "yield_potential": 4.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Sakas is a horse gram (kulthi) variety released in 2016 by AICRP on DLA, Solapur, MPKV, Rahuri. It is an early-maturing variety with a crop duration of 90-95 days. The grain is brown in colour. In terms of quality, the grain contains 22.09% crude protein and 37.86 mg/100g iron. The yield is 8-10 q/ha. This variety is recommended for cultivation on light soils in Maharashtra state.", "label_hi": "कुलथी फुले सकस", "label_mr": "कुळीथ फुले सकस", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Light soil"], "protein_content": "22.09%", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra state", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "90-95 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "8-10 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a9202d1e-5f5d-429b-841d-d362342d8ffe", "maturity_days_min": 115, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 3.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Seena is a horse gram (kulthi) variety released in 1984 by AICRP on DLA, Solapur, MPKV, Rahuri. The crop duration of this variety is 115-120 days. Its grain is brick red in colour. The yield of this variety is 6-8 q/ha. Seena is recommended for cultivation on light soils in Maharashtra state.", "label_hi": "कुलथी सीना", "label_mr": "कुळीथ सीना", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Light soil"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra state", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "115-120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "6-8 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "cafae537-c4d0-4f28-b6f7-0107fb1a5343", "maturity_days_min": 240, "maturity_days_max": 255, "yield_potential": 11.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "NDA 1 x MAL 13", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPA 15-2 (Sharada) was released in 2020 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur, from the cross NDA 1 x MAL 13. It is a long-duration variety that flowers in 150-158 days and matures in 240-255 days. The plant is compact, 240-270 cm tall, with a green stem, no hairs on the leaves, 20-24 primary branches and 295-354 pods per plant. The flower has a yellow base, and the outer layer of the standard petal is red. Seeds are brown and medium in size, with a creamy brown, smooth seed coat and a 100-seed weight of 10-12 g. Crude grain protein is 19%. Yield is 28 q/ha. It is recommended for the North Eastern Plain Zone (Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Chhattisgarh, West Bengal) under rainfed or irrigated conditions. It is resistant to Fusarium wilt and sterility mosaic disease (SMD).", "label_hi": "अरहर IPA 15-2 (शारदा)", "label_mr": "तूर IPA 15-2 (शारदा)", "aes": {"flowering_days": "150-158 days", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "protein_content": "19%", "recommended_areas_published": "North Eastern Plain Zone: UP, Bihar, Chhattisgarh, West Bengal", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "240-255 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "28 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "bb6550d6-f2bc-4780-8ece-47c25ee8624c", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 7.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPA 15-6 is a pigeon pea variety developed by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. Its yield is 19 q/ha. The variety is resistant to two diseases, Fusarium wilt and sterility mosaic disease (SMD). It is recommended for the Central Zone, which covers Madhya Pradesh, Rajasthan, Gujarat, Maharashtra and Chhattisgarh.", "label_hi": "अरहर IPA 15-6", "label_mr": "तूर IPA 15-6", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Central zone: MP, Rajasthan, Gujarat, Maharashtra, Chhattisgarh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "19 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "d45305fb-6d9e-4b31-ac5e-79476155723a", "maturity_days_min": 164, "maturity_days_max": 166, "yield_potential": 9.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Kaveri was released in 2022 by the Pulses Improvement Project, MPKV, Rahuri. It belongs to the mid-early duration group, with a crop duration of 164-166 days. The seeds are light brown and bold, with a 100-seed weight of 11.52 g. Yield is 24.41 q/ha. It is recommended for Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh and Telangana, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm. The variety is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt and sterility mosaic disease (SMD).", "label_hi": "अरहर फुले कावेरी", "label_mr": "तूर फुले कावेरी", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "164-166 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "24.41 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a1d1ca34-6193-40c3-96f7-38c806f03209", "maturity_days_min": 157, "maturity_days_max": 159, "yield_potential": 8.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Pallavi (PT-12-19-2) was released in 2024 by the Pulses Improvement Project, MPKV, Rahuri, under ICAR-AICRP on Pulses. It is an open-pollinated (OPV), mid-early maturing variety for the kharif season, with a crop duration of 157-159 days. The grains are light brown and bold, with a 100-seed weight of 11.00 g. Yield is 21.45 q/ha. It is recommended for the Central Zone (Maharashtra, Gujarat, Madhya Pradesh, Rajasthan and Chhattisgarh) under rainfed or irrigated conditions, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm. The variety is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt and sterility mosaic disease (SMD), and shows less incidence of pod borer and pod fly.", "label_hi": "अरहर फुले पल्लवी (PT-12-19-2)", "label_mr": "तूर फुले पल्लवी (PT-12-19-2)", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Central zone (Maharashtra, Gujarat, Madhya Pradesh, Rajasthan and Chhattisgarh)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "157-159 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "21.45 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "37153dd3-41c8-4a41-8888-45bbc62ce21c", "maturity_days_min": 135, "maturity_days_max": 150, "yield_potential": 12.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Rajeshwari was released in 2012 by the Pulses Improvement Project, MPKV, Rahuri. It is an early-maturing variety with a crop duration of 135-150 days. The seeds are dark brown and medium bold, with a 100-seed weight of 10.5 to 11.0 g. Yield is 28-30 q/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh and Gujarat, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm. The variety is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt and sterility mosaic disease (SMD).", "label_hi": "अरहर फुले राजेश्वरी", "label_mr": "तूर फुले राजेश्वरी", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Gujarat", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "135-150 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "28-30 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "e7de409f-6f9c-481e-90f6-608b9d2e8ec9", "maturity_days_min": 167, "maturity_days_max": 169, "yield_potential": 13.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Trupti was released in 2022 by the Pulses Improvement Project, MPKV, Rahuri. It belongs to the mid-early duration group, with a crop duration of 167-169 days. The seeds are light brown and bold, with a 100-seed weight of 10.81 g. Yield is 32.03 q/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Gujarat and Chhattisgarh, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm. The variety is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt and sterility mosaic disease (SMD).", "label_hi": "अरहर फुले तृप्ति", "label_mr": "तूर फुले तृप्ती", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh, Gujarat, Chhattisgarh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "167-169 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "32.03 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3a24619b-0a1a-4844-99a9-d1be625f71c7", "maturity_days_min": 176, "maturity_days_max": 176, "yield_potential": 8.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PKV Tara (PKV-TAT-9629) was released in 2013 by Dr. PDKV, Akola. The crop duration is 176 days. The seeds are red and medium bold. Yield is 18-20 q/ha. It is recommended for the Vidarbha region of Maharashtra. The variety is resistant to Fusarium wilt and moderately resistant to sterility mosaic disease (SMD).", "label_hi": "अरहर PKV तारा (PKV-TAT-9629)", "label_mr": "तूर PKV तारा (PKV-TAT-9629)", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Vidarbha region of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "176 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "18-20 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "13d81ae1-8fc9-4e88-a80f-cb0125c20a5f", "maturity_days_min": 140, "maturity_days_max": 145, "yield_potential": 9.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "8(E)", "notification_date": "2021-12-24", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pusa Arhar 2018-4 was released in 2021 by ICAR-IARI, New Delhi, and notified vide S.O. 8(E) dated 2021-12-24. It matures in 140-145 days. The mean 100-seed weight is 8.73 g, and the seeds are bolder than other varieties released for the North Western Plain Zone (NWPZ). Seed protein is 22.75%. Yield is 23.06 q/ha. It is recommended for the NWPZ (Punjab, Delhi, Haryana and Western Uttar Pradesh) and is suitable for the pigeon pea-wheat rotation. Compared with susceptible check varieties, it showed lower incidence of Fusarium wilt, sterility mosaic disease (SMD) and Phytophthora blight.", "label_hi": "अरहर पूसा अरहर 2018-4", "label_mr": "तूर पूसा अरहर 2018-4", "aes": {"protein_content": "22.75 %", "recommended_areas_published": "NWPZ (Punjab, Delhi, Haryana, Western Uttar Pradesh); suitable for pigeonpea-wheat rotation", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "140-145 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "23.06 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ef5dd4ea-f620-4f01-8d33-0aed25c885a9", "maturity_days_min": 160, "maturity_days_max": 170, "yield_potential": 12.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Vipula was released in 2006 by the Pulses Improvement Project, MPKV, Rahuri. The crop duration is 160-170 days. The seeds are red and medium in size. Yield is 28-30 q/ha. It is recommended for Maharashtra, on well-drained, medium to deep soils with a depth of 45 to 60 cm. The variety is resistant to Fusarium wilt and moderately resistant to sterility mosaic disease (SMD).", "label_hi": "अरहर विपुला", "label_mr": "तूर विपुला", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Well drained, medium to deep soils having 45 to 60 cm depth"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "160-170 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "28-30 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2bd50675-88a0-4c38-8fba-5e6c6a590e50", "maturity_days_min": 80, "maturity_days_max": 85, "yield_potential": 4.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPU 11-02 is a black gram (urad) variety released in 2019 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. Crop duration is 80-85 days. Seeds are dull black and medium large, with a 100-seed weight of 4.3 g. Protein content is 26%. Yield is 10-12 q/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for Madhya Pradesh and Uttar Pradesh. It is resistant to yellow mosaic (MYMV), leaf crinkle (ULCV), powdery mildew, anthracnose and Cercospora leaf spot.", "label_hi": "उड़द IPU 11-02", "label_mr": "उडीद IPU 11-02", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "protein_content": "26%", "recommended_areas_published": "Madhya Pradesh and Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "80-85 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10-12 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "921e6277-5c69-4af3-b1d4-c6af3049f62b", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 75, "yield_potential": 4.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2020, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPU 13-1 is a black gram (urad) variety released in 2020 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur. Crop duration is 70-75 days. Seeds are dull black and medium large, with a 100-seed weight of 4.14 g. Protein content is 26%. Yield is 10-12 q/ha. It is recommended for Madhya Pradesh and Uttar Pradesh. It is resistant to yellow mosaic (MYMV), Cercospora leaf spot, leaf crinkle (ULCV), sunflower necrosis disease, web blight, bacterial blight, anthracnose and powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "उड़द IPU 13-1", "label_mr": "उडीद IPU 13-1", "aes": {"protein_content": "26%", "recommended_areas_published": "Madhya Pradesh and Uttar Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70-75 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10-12 q/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "267b2adf-4a3c-4e0e-a700-b13b3963619b", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 6.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Pant Urd 10 is a black gram (urad) variety released in 2018 by G.B. Pant University of Agriculture & Technology, Pantnagar, under the AICRP-MULLaRP programme. It gives a yield of 12-15 q/ha. This variety is meant for the kharif season. It is recommended for the North Hill Zone of India, which covers the hills of Jammu & Kashmir, Himachal, Uttarakhand and the North East states of India.", "label_hi": "उड़द पंत उर्द 10", "label_mr": "उडीद पंत उर्द 10", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "recommended_areas_published": "North Hill Zone of India (Hills of J & K, Himachal, Uttarakhand and North East States of India)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "12-15 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "f5a3f681-bc67-4c77-b606-731a6cdcae69", "maturity_days_min": 77, "maturity_days_max": 77, "yield_potential": 3.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Rajan is a black gram (urad) variety released in 2022 by MPKV (Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth), Rahuri. Crop duration is 77 days. It has bright, bold, black seed with a 100-seed weight of 3.92 g. Yield is 8.32 q/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for Maharashtra and suits medium to deep soils. It is moderately tolerant to powdery mildew and yellow mosaic (MYMV).", "label_hi": "उड़द फुले राजन", "label_mr": "उडीद फुले राजन", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium to Deep"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "77 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "8.32 q ha-1", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "c96f6fca-94ea-42e3-bfba-6c7c8a445abe", "maturity_days_min": 73, "maturity_days_max": 73, "yield_potential": 3.5, "yield_rainfed": 3.5, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Vasu is a black gram (urad) variety released in 2021 by MPKV (Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth), Rahuri. Crop duration is 73 days. The seeds are bold, with a 100-seed weight of 4.87 g. Yield is 8.59 q/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for Maharashtra under rainfed conditions and suits medium to deep soils. It is tolerant to powdery mildew and yellow mosaic (MYMV).", "label_hi": "उड़द फुले वसु", "label_mr": "उडीद फुले वसू", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "soil_types": ["Medium to Deep"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra (rainfed conditions)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "73 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "8.59 q ha-1", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "e1853f10-badc-42a4-be4e-13d2d7b37df0", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 75, "yield_potential": 4.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "TPU-4 is a black gram (urad) variety released in 1992 by BARC, Mumbai and the Pulses Improvement Project, MPKV Rahuri. Crop duration is 70-75 days. Plants are tall and semi-spreading, with profuse branching and broad leaves. Seeds are bold. Yield is 10-12 q/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for all the districts of Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh and Gujarat, and suits medium to black cotton soils. It is tolerant to powdery mildew and yellow mosaic (MYMV).", "label_hi": "उड़द TPU-4", "label_mr": "उडीद TPU-4", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium to Black Cotton Soil"], "recommended_areas_published": "all the districts of Maharashtra, Madhya Pradesh and Gujrat (Kharif)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70-75 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10-12 q ha-1", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "1fa0552b-2f9b-4dfb-859d-2ecd3f21bb28", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 75, "yield_potential": 4.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": 4.6, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Vamban 1 x UH 04-04", "notification_number": "3220(E)", "notification_date": "2019-09-05", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "VBN 10 is a black gram (urad) variety released in 2019 by the National Pulses Research Centre, Vamban (TNAU), from the cross Vamban 1 x UH 04-04. It was notified under S.O. 3220(E) dated 2019-09-05. Crop duration is 70-75 days. Plants are determinate, mature at the same time and grow 35-40 cm tall. Pods are hairy and the 100-grain weight is 4.0-5.0 g. Yield is 1130 kg/ha under irrigation. It is a rabi variety recommended for the South zone states of Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka and Odisha. It is resistant to yellow mosaic (MYMV), leaf crinkle (ULCV) and leaf curl virus.", "label_hi": "उड़द VBN 10", "label_mr": "उडीद VBN 10", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "recommended_areas_published": "South zone states viz., Andra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka and Odisha (rabi)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70-75 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "1130 kg/ha (irrigated)", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "c990b80c-d60c-4f02-9078-396d25ac362b", "maturity_days_min": 65, "maturity_days_max": 70, "yield_potential": 4.0, "yield_rainfed": 3.5, "yield_irrigated": 4.0, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Vamban 3 x VBN 04-008", "notification_number": "1379(E)", "notification_date": "2018-03-27", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "VBN 8 is a black gram (urad) variety released in 2016 by the National Pulses Research Centre, Vamban (TNAU), from the cross Vamban 3 x VBN 04-008. It was notified under S.O. 1379(E) dated 2018-03-27. Crop duration is 65-70 days. Plants are determinate and non-shattering, mature at the same time and grow 35-40 cm tall. Pods are hairy and the 100-grain weight is 4.5-5.0 g. Protein content is 21.9% and arabinose content is 7.5%. Yield is 988 kg/ha under irrigation. It is a central release for the summer irrigated season in Odisha, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka and Tamil Nadu, and can be grown rainfed or irrigated. It is resistant to yellow mosaic (MYMV) and leaf crinkle (ULCV), and moderately resistant to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "उड़द VBN 8", "label_mr": "उडीद VBN 8", "aes": {"season": "summer", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "protein_content": "21.9%", "recommended_areas_published": "Orissa, Andra Pradesh, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu (central release, summer irrigated season)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "65-70 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "988 kg/ha (irrigated)", "season_published": "summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "82538d94-dafc-4cb0-acac-f746d5cd72c7", "maturity_days_min": 60, "maturity_days_max": 65, "yield_potential": 6.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPM 410-3 (Shikha) is a green gram (moong) variety released in 2016 by ICAR-IIPR (Indian Institute of Pulses Research), Kanpur. Crop duration is 60-65 days. Yield is 13-16 q/ha. It is suited to the summer and spring seasons and is recommended for the North West Plain Zone and the Central Zone. It is highly resistant to yellow mosaic (MYMV), powdery mildew and Cercospora leaf spot.", "label_hi": "मूंग IPM 410-3 (शिखा)", "label_mr": "मूग IPM 410-3 (शिखा)", "aes": {"season": "summer", "recommended_areas_published": "North West Plain Zone, Central Zone", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "60-65 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "13-16 q/ha", "season_published": "summer, spring", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "3f66f089-ca53-490e-9922-9f20146316c9", "maturity_days_min": 65, "maturity_days_max": 70, "yield_potential": 6.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "IPM 99-125/Co 5", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "IPM 512-1 (Soorya) is a green gram (moong) variety released in 2020 by ICAR-Indian Institute of Pulses Research, Kanpur, from the cross IPM 99-125/Co 5. Crop duration is 65-70 days. Seeds are green, shining and attractive, medium-large in size, with a 100-seed weight of 3.9 g. Protein content is 21.53%. Yield is 14-16 q/ha. It is recommended for the North East Plain Zone in the spring season. It is highly resistant to yellow mosaic (MYMV) and anthracnose, and moderately resistant to Cercospora leaf spot.", "label_hi": "मूंग IPM 512-1 (सूर्या)", "label_mr": "मूग IPM 512-1 (सूर्या)", "aes": {"protein_content": "21.53 %", "recommended_areas_published": "North East Plain Zone (spring season)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "65-70 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "14-16 q/ha", "season_published": "spring", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "dad7a82e-aecf-4638-a69a-63a9fa5a6479", "maturity_days_min": 74, "maturity_days_max": 74, "yield_potential": 4.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Lam Pesara 610 (LGG 610) is a green gram (moong) variety released in 2024 by ICAR-AICRP on Pulses, RARS, Lam, Guntur, Acharya N.G. Ranga Agricultural University, Andhra Pradesh. It matures in 74 days. The crop is suitable for mechanical harvesting. Protein content is 23.16%. Yield is 11.17 q/ha. It is a rabi variety recommended for the South zone states of Andhra Pradesh, Telangana, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Kerala and Odisha, in rice fallows and upland conditions. It is resistant to yellow mosaic (MYMV).", "label_hi": "मूंग लाम पेसरा 610 (LGG 610)", "label_mr": "मूग लाम पेसरा 610 (LGG 610)", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "protein_content": "23.16%", "recommended_areas_published": "South zone states, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana, Tamilnadu, Karnataka, Kerala and Odisha; rabi; rice fallows and upland conditions", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "74 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "11.17 q/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "8f68578a-d42c-431e-9c44-73cbc5d55531", "maturity_days_min": 65, "maturity_days_max": 69, "yield_potential": 4.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "SML-668 X Naval (pedigree selection)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Chetak (PM-707-5) is a green gram (moong) variety released in 2020 by the Oilseeds Research Station, MPKV, Jalgaon. It was developed by pedigree selection from the cross SML-668 x Naval. It flowers in 39 days and crop duration is 65-69 days. Plants are on average 56.84 cm tall, with dark green leaves and a green, hairy stem, and carry 24.60 pods per plant. Seeds are bold, with a 100-seed weight of 4.77 g. Dry seed protein is 25.60% and germinated seed protein is 21.88%. Nitrogen content is 4.10%. Yield is 10 q/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for Maharashtra and suits medium to deep soils. It is moderately resistant to powdery mildew and yellow mosaic (MYMV).", "label_hi": "मूंग फुले चेतक (PM-707-5)", "label_mr": "मूग फुले चेतक (PM-707-5)", "aes": {"flowering_days": "39 days", "season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium to Deep"], "protein_content": "25.60%", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra (kharif)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "65-69 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10 q ha-1", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "47f1cfdd-8f91-47a6-979b-d9e4140e56da", "maturity_days_min": 60, "maturity_days_max": 65, "yield_potential": 4.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule M-2 is a green gram (moong) variety released in 1989 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. Crop duration is 60-65 days. Seeds are green and medium in size, with a 100-seed weight of 3.6-3.8 g. Yield is 8-10 q/ha. This variety is suited to the kharif and summer seasons and is recommended for Western Maharashtra, on medium black soils.", "label_hi": "मूंग फुले M-2", "label_mr": "मूग फुले M-2", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium black"], "recommended_areas_published": "W. Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "60-65 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "8-10 q ha-1", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b9feed8c-4338-4e2e-8e66-6c12f015924c", "maturity_days_min": 70, "maturity_days_max": 70, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": "OPV", "description": "PMS-8 is a green gram (moong) variety. It was released in 2024 by the Division of Genetics of ICAR-Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI), New Delhi. It is an open-pollinated variety (OPV). The crop reaches maturity in 70 days. The variety is suitable for growing under saline conditions. It is recommended for cultivation by farmers in the National Capital Region of Delhi.", "label_hi": "मूंग PMS-8", "label_mr": "मूग PMS-8", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "National Capital Region of Delhi", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "70 days (days to maturity)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "99c431d9-8887-4fa8-ab03-a97caf1a3ebf", "maturity_days_min": 69, "maturity_days_max": 74, "yield_potential": 5.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Vaibhav is a green gram (moong) variety released in 2001 by the Pulses Improvement Project, MPKV Rahuri. Crop duration is 69-74 days. Plants are tall and semi-spreading with profuse branching, a green stem with light pigmentation, and broad leaves with a brown midrib. It bears long pods with bold seeds. Yield is 12-14 q/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for all the districts of Maharashtra and suits medium to black cotton soils. It is resistant to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "मूंग वैभव", "label_mr": "मूग वैभव", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium to Black Cotton Soil"], "recommended_areas_published": "all the districts of Maharashtra (Kharif)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "69-74 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "12-14 q ha-1", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2b069cc3-4121-4e2c-b287-da42ce58608e", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 130, "yield_potential": 2.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "MBS-27 is a moth bean variety. It was released in 1989 by the AICRP on DLA, Solapur, under MPKV (Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth), Rahuri. The total crop duration of this variety is 120-130 days. Its grain is brown in colour. It gives a yield of 6-7 q/ha. The variety is recommended for cultivation in Maharashtra state, and it is suited to light soil.", "label_hi": "मोठ MBS-27", "label_mr": "मटकी MBS-27", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Light soil"], "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra state", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-130 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "6-7 q ha-1", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "105ca8bc-51be-4b8e-ac69-f1b8d964f1ce", "maturity_days_min": 75, "maturity_days_max": 77, "yield_potential": 6.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Rukmini (PCP 0306-1) is a cowpea variety released in 2016 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. Its crop duration is 75-77 days. It is an early variety with an indeterminate, erect growth habit and dark green, medium-size leaflets, and the crop does not lodge. The seeds are pearly white and kidney-shaped. The yield is 10-15 q/ha. It can be grown year-round, including the kharif and summer seasons. Under central release for the South zone, it is suitable for the multiple cropping system of the south zone of India. It suits medium to deep soils and can be grown under rainfed or irrigated conditions.", "label_hi": "लोबिया फुले रुक्मिणी (PCP 0306-1)", "label_mr": "चवळी फुले रुक्मिणी (PCP 0306-1)", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Medium to Deep soils"], "recommended_areas_published": "Suitable for multiple cropping system of south zone of India (central release, South zone)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "75-77 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10-15 q ha-1", "season_published": "year-round, kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "591a9c06-fd38-495c-a1f4-4fcadd28cb3b", "maturity_days_min": 65, "maturity_days_max": 72, "yield_potential": 10.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Vithai (PCP 05040) is a cowpea variety released in 2015 by Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth (MPKV), Rahuri. Its crop duration is 65-72 days. It is an early variety with an indeterminate, erect growth habit, dark green, medium-size leaflets and dark purple flowers, and the crop does not lodge. The seeds are off-white and kidney-shaped. The yield is 15-25 q/ha. It can be grown year-round, including the kharif and summer seasons, and is recommended for the cropping system of Western Maharashtra. It suits medium to deep soils and can be grown under rainfed or irrigated conditions.", "label_hi": "लोबिया फुले विठाई (PCP 05040)", "label_mr": "चवळी फुले विठाई (PCP 05040)", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Medium to Deep soils"], "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra cropping system", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "65-72 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "15-25 q ha-1", "season_published": "year-round, kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "efd00a9b-e8ce-46d4-8971-847790f3b3ca", "maturity_days_min": 55, "maturity_days_max": 65, "yield_potential": 3.8, "yield_rainfed": 3.8, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Pureline selection from IT 85-F2020", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Vamban 1 is a cowpea variety released in 1997 by the National Pulses Research Centre, Vamban (TNAU). It is a pureline selection from IT 85-F2020. It flowers in 35-40 days and has a crop duration of 55-65 days. The plants are 25-30 cm tall, with an erect green stem, 2-4 branches and light green leaves. The pods are greenish white and the grains are white, with a 100-grain weight of 12-15 g. The yield is 950 kg/ha under rainfed conditions. It is recommended for rainfed cultivation throughout Tamil Nadu.", "label_hi": "लोबिया वंबन 1", "label_mr": "चवळी वंबन 1", "aes": {"flowering_days": "35-40 days", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "recommended_areas_published": "Throughout Tamil Nadu (rainfed)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "55-65 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "950 kg/ha (rainfed)", "season_published": "Adipattam (June-August)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a7b63c26-0f9a-4676-ac5c-1714724703a6", "maturity_days_min": 105, "maturity_days_max": 110, "yield_potential": 14.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": 14.2, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "summer"], "parentage": "Derivative of a complex cross [(ICGV 92069 x ICGV 93184)SIL4 x ICGV 98300]; bred by ICRISAT, identified by MPKV Jalgaon", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2017, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Bharati (JL 776) is an open-pollinated (OPV) groundnut variety bred by ICRISAT and identified by MPKV through its Oilseeds Research Station, Jalgaon; it was released in 2017. It is derived from the complex cross [(ICGV 92069 x ICGV 93184)SIL4 x ICGV 98300] and belongs to the Spanish bunch group (Arachis hypogaea ssp. fastigiata var. vulgaris). Its crop duration is 105-110 days. The 100-kernel weight is 35 g, the shelling out-turn is 69% and sound mature kernels are 92%. The oil content is 51%. The yield is 30-35 q/ha. It is grown in the kharif and summer seasons, and under central release it is recommended for the rabi-summer season in Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh (Zone III). It suits medium to light soils. It is highly resistant to tobacco caterpillar (Spodoptera litura) and rust, and moderately resistant to late leaf spot.", "label_hi": "मूंगफली फुले भारती (JL 776)", "label_mr": "भुईमूग फुले भारती (JL 776)", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Medium to light"], "oil_content": "51%", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra and Madhya Pradesh (Zone III), rabi-summer (central release)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "105-110 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "30-35 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "8ef88065-1f3d-49f3-90a5-1ce22be7f1a7", "maturity_days_min": 105, "maturity_days_max": 110, "yield_potential": 9.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Chaitanya (KDG 160) is a groundnut variety released in 2016 by the Agricultural Research Station, K. Digraj, Dist. Sangli (MPKV). Its crop duration is 105-110 days. It has medium bold kernels with a 100-kernel weight of 40-48 g, and the shelling is 65-69%. The oil content is 51.6%. The yield is 20-24 q/ha. It is a summer-season variety grown under irrigation and is recommended for the rabi-summer season in Andhra Pradesh, Telangana and Tamil Nadu. It suits light to medium sandy loam soils with high organic matter content and a pH of 7 to 8. It is moderately resistant to stem rot and late leaf spot.", "label_hi": "मूंगफली फुले चैतन्य (KDG 160)", "label_mr": "भुईमूग फुले चैतन्य (KDG 160)", "aes": {"season": "summer", "irrigation_regime": "irrigated", "soil_types": ["Light to medium sandy loam with high organic matter content, pH- 7 to 8"], "oil_content": "51.6%", "recommended_areas_published": "Rabi-summer in Andhra Pradesh, Telangana & Tamilnadu", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "105-110 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "20-24 q/ha", "season_published": "summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "53096a8a-5bc8-43ae-95ce-15e2c7294fd8", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 125, "yield_potential": 12.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Derivative of a cross ICGV 96050 X ICGV 96239; bred by ICRISAT, identified by MPKV Digraj", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2017, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Morna (KDG 123) is an open-pollinated (OPV) groundnut variety bred by ICRISAT and identified by MPKV through its Agricultural Research Station, K. Digraj, Dist. Sangli; it was released in 2017. It comes from the cross ICGV 96050 x ICGV 96239 and belongs to the Virginia bunch group (Arachis hypogaea ssp. hypogaea var. hypogaea). Its crop duration is 120-125 days. It has medium bold kernels with a 100-kernel weight of 43-52 g and a shelling out-turn of 68-70%. The oil content is 46-48%. The yield is 25-30 q/ha. This kharif variety is recommended for Gujarat and south Rajasthan (Zone II); Odisha, West Bengal, Jharkhand and Imphal (Zone IV); and Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka and southern Maharashtra (Zone V). It suits light to medium sandy loam soils with high organic matter content and a pH of 7 to 8. It is moderately resistant to late leaf spot and rust.", "label_hi": "मूंगफली फुले मोरणा (KDG 123)", "label_mr": "भुईमूग फुले मोरणा (KDG 123)", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Light to medium sandy loam with high organic matter content, pH- 7 to 8"], "oil_content": "46-48 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Gujarat and south Rajasthan (Zone II); Odisha, West Bengal, Jharkhand, Imphal (Zone IV); Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka, southern Maharashtra (Zone V)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-125 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "25-30 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "e3bfd14b-fbe0-4fa3-b973-fa552134faf4", "maturity_days_min": 115, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 12.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Derivative of a complex cross [(ICGV 87121 X ICGV 87853) X ICGV 92023) X ICGV 98300)]; bred by ICRISAT, identified by MPKV Digraj", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2017, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Warna (KDG 128) is an open-pollinated (OPV) groundnut variety bred by ICRISAT, identified by MPKV's Agricultural Research Station, K. Digraj, Dist. Sangli, and released in 2017. It comes from a complex cross of ICGV 87121, ICGV 87853, ICGV 92023 and ICGV 98300. It is a Virginia bunch type (Arachis hypogaea ssp. hypogaea var. hypogaea) with stay-green foliage. Its crop duration is 115-120 days. Kernels are medium bold, with a 100-kernel weight of 40-55 g, shelling out-turn of 64-69% and 89-92% sound mature kernels. Oil content is 50% and oil yield 1225-1470 kg/ha. The yield is 25-30 q/ha. This kharif variety is recommended for Gujarat and south Rajasthan (Zone II) and Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka and southern Maharashtra (Zone V). It suits light to medium sandy loam soils with high organic matter and pH 7 to 8. It is moderately resistant to late leaf spot and rust.", "label_hi": "मूंगफली फुले वारणा (KDG 128)", "label_mr": "भुईमूग फुले वारणा (KDG 128)", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "soil_types": ["Light to medium sandy loam with high organic matter content, pH- 7 to 8"], "oil_content": "49%", "recommended_areas_published": "Gujarat and south Rajasthan (Zone II); Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka, southern Maharashtra (Zone V)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "115-120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "25-30 q/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "fbb42fa0-04cb-47ea-b7a8-052f2f0b7ead", "maturity_days_min": 97, "maturity_days_max": 97, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "1056(E)", "notification_date": "2023-03-06", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "JS 21-72 is an open-pollinated (OPV) soybean variety released in 2023 by JNKVV, Jabalpur. It was notified under S.O. 1056(E) dated 2023-03-06. The variety matures in 97 days. It is recommended for cultivation in the Central Zone.", "label_hi": "सोयाबीन JS 21-72", "label_mr": "सोयाबीन JS 21-72", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "97 days (days to maturity)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "cd60ab4b-bd53-4367-a45a-0395adba4a3a", "maturity_days_min": 100, "maturity_days_max": 100, "yield_potential": 8.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "500(E)", "notification_date": "2021-01-29", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "MACS 1520 is an open-pollinated (OPV) soybean variety released in 2021 by ARI, Pune, and notified under S.O. 500(E) dated 2021-01-29. It matures in 100 days. Its pods do not shatter, and it is suitable for mechanical harvesting. The yield is 2149 kg/ha. It is recommended for the Central Zone: Madhya Pradesh, the Bundelkhand region of Uttar Pradesh, Rajasthan, Gujarat, and the Marathwada and Vidarbha regions of Maharashtra. It is resistant to charcoal rot, yellow mosaic virus (YMV), bacterial pustule, Rhizoctonia aerial blight and Alternaria leaf spot. It is highly resistant to stem fly, girdle beetle, defoliators, leafhopper, stink bug, bean bug and pod borer.", "label_hi": "सोयाबीन MACS 1520", "label_mr": "सोयाबीन MACS 1520", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone: Madhya Pradesh, Bundelkhand Region of UP, Rajasthan, Gujarat, Marathwada and Vidarbha Regions of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "100 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "2149 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "4375d6c1-9ab0-405c-bf78-00ffbcee6a9f", "maturity_days_min": 92, "maturity_days_max": 92, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "500(E)", "notification_date": "2021-01-29", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "NRC 130 is an open-pollinated (OPV) soybean variety released in 2021 by ICAR-IISR, Indore, and notified under S.O. 500(E) dated 2021-01-29. It is an early-maturing variety that matures in 92 days. It carries the photo-insensitive allele e3. The plants are 47.4 cm tall and suited to mechanical harvesting. It is recommended for the Central Zone and can be grown under rainfed or irrigated conditions. It is moderately resistant to charcoal rot and pod blight (Colletotrichum), and resistant to stem fly, girdle beetle and defoliators.", "label_hi": "सोयाबीन NRC 130", "label_mr": "सोयाबीन NRC 130", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "92 days (days to maturity)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "93bcbb7d-f1bb-4dd0-a349-07f44cc06610", "maturity_days_min": 93, "maturity_days_max": 93, "yield_potential": 7.2, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "2986(E)", "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "NRC 138 is an open-pollinated (OPV) soybean variety released in 2021 by ICAR-IISR, Indore, and notified under S.O. 2986(E). It matures in 93 days. The plants have a determinate growth habit, pointed ovate leaves, white flowers and dark brown pubescence. The pods are brown and the hilum is brown. The yield is 1789 kg/ha. It is recommended for the Central Zone and can be grown under rainfed or irrigated conditions. It is resistant to yellow mosaic virus (YMV) and moderately resistant to pod blight (Colletotrichum) and target leaf spot, but it is susceptible to charcoal rot, Rhizoctonia aerial blight and Myrothecium leaf spot.", "label_hi": "सोयाबीन NRC 138", "label_mr": "सोयाबीन NRC 138", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "93 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "1789 kg /ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "6e6d7d92-b892-45f1-8cfb-5a4ef6a4b2fa", "maturity_days_min": 97, "maturity_days_max": 97, "yield_potential": 8.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "2986(E)", "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "NRC 142 is an open-pollinated (OPV) soybean variety released in 2021 by ICAR-IISR, Indore, and notified under S.O. 2986(E). It matures in 97 days. The plants have a determinate growth habit, purple flowers, dark green ovate leaves and brown pubescence, and their good height makes them suitable for mechanical harvesting. The seeds are oval with a black hilum. It is a food-grade variety, free from lipoxygenase-2 (LOX 2) and Kunitz trypsin inhibitor (KTi). The yield is 2200 kg/ha. It is recommended for the Central Zone and the Southern Zone and can be grown under rainfed or irrigated conditions. It is resistant to yellow mosaic virus (YMV) and moderately resistant to Rhizoctonia aerial blight and target leaf spot.", "label_hi": "सोयाबीन NRC 142", "label_mr": "सोयाबीन NRC 142", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone and Southern Zone", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "97 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "2200 kg /ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "51d77290-5690-4457-8f83-4552e96bde7d", "maturity_days_min": 90, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 7.1, "yield_rainfed": 7.1, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Developed through MAS (marker-assisted selection) for freedom from Lipoxygenase-2; parents not stated", "notification_number": "1056(E)", "notification_date": "2023-03-06", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "NRC 150 is an open-pollinated (OPV) soybean variety released in 2023 by ICAR-IISR, Indore, and notified under S.O. 1056(E) dated 2023-03-06. It was developed through marker-assisted selection (MAS) to be free from lipoxygenase-2. It matures in 90 days. The plants have a semi-determinate growth habit, white flowers, green leaves and brown pubescence on the plant and pods, and they are amenable to mechanical harvesting. The hilum is black. The yield is 1757.5 kg/ha under rainfed conditions. It is recommended for rainfed cultivation in the Central Zone. It is highly resistant to charcoal rot and moderately resistant to yellow mosaic virus (YMV) and defoliators.", "label_hi": "सोयाबीन NRC 150", "label_mr": "सोयाबीन NRC 150", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "90 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "1757.5 kg /ha (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "59a2bd70-6d03-4012-8bc5-e5740c080872", "maturity_days_min": 90, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": "1056(E)", "notification_date": "2023-03-06", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "NRC 152 is an open-pollinated (OPV) soybean variety released in 2023 by ICAR-IISR, Indore, and notified under S.O. 1056(E) dated 2023-03-06. It matures in 90 days. It is free from Kunitz trypsin inhibitor (KTI) and from lipoxygenase-2. It is recommended for cultivation in the Central Zone.", "label_hi": "सोयाबीन NRC 152", "label_mr": "सोयाबीन NRC 152", "aes": {"recommended_areas_published": "Central Zone", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "90 days (days to maturity)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "8fe8d496-a63b-4b02-989e-bc624af1191a", "maturity_days_min": 95, "maturity_days_max": 100, "yield_potential": 2.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Karala (IGPN-2004-1) is an open-pollinated niger variety released by ZARS, Igatpuri, Nashik (MPKV). The crop duration is 95-100 days. It has bold seeds of a shiny black colour. The oil content is 39% and the linoleic acid content is 62.1%, which is more than IGP-76. Yield is 450-500 kg/ha. It is recommended for the high rainfall areas of Maharashtra and Karnataka states, on light to medium black soils. It is tolerant to Alternaria leaf spot and powdery mildew, and resistant to lodging.", "label_hi": "रामतिल फुले कारला (IGPN-2004-1)", "label_mr": "कारळे फुले कारळा (IGPN-2004-1)", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Light to medium black"], "oil_content": "39%", "recommended_areas_published": "High rainfall areas of Maharashtra and Karnataka states", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "95-100 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "450-500 Kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "9e61f131-c401-4ee7-8a36-eadefeb29d66", "maturity_days_min": 135, "maturity_days_max": 140, "yield_potential": 5.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "A-300; breeding method: Selection", "notification_number": "2(E)814(E)", "notification_date": "1983-01-03", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Bhima (S-4) is an open-pollinated safflower variety released in 1982 by the Dry Farming Research Station, Solapur, Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth, Rahuri, and notified in 1983. It was developed by selection from A-300. It flowers in 75-80 days and matures in 135-140 days. The flowers are white at bloom and turn dirty white with a red spot when faded. The seed oil content is 28-30%. Yield is 1400 kg/ha. It is recommended for Western Maharashtra on medium deep to deep soils. It is tolerant to drought and moderately tolerant to aphid and Fusarium wilt.", "label_hi": "कुसुम भीमा (S-4)", "label_mr": "करडई भीमा (S-4)", "aes": {"flowering_days": "75-80 days", "soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "28-30 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Western Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "135-140 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "1400 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "0eb0bcc0-6a71-4509-a404-463b54fb929c", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 125, "yield_potential": 6.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Selection from GMU-7368", "notification_number": "3482(E)", "notification_date": "2020-10-07", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "CG Kusum-1 is an open-pollinated safflower variety released in 2020 by the AICRP (Safflower) centre, Indira Gandhi Krishi Vishwavidyalaya, Raipur, and notified in the same year. It was developed by selection from GMU-7368. It flowers in 80-85 days and matures in 120-125 days. The oil content of the seed is 32-33%. Yield is 1677 kg/ha. It is recommended for growing in the Chhattisgarh plains.", "label_hi": "कुसुम CG कुसुम-1", "label_mr": "करडई CG कुसुम-1", "aes": {"flowering_days": "80-85 days", "oil_content": "32-33%", "recommended_areas_published": "Chhattisgarh plains", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-125 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "1677 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "bce906bf-9e4f-4dc8-8a07-8ff9443e539d", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": null, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PBNS-184 is an open-pollinated safflower variety from the AICRP on Safflower, Vasantrao Naik Marathwada Krishi Vidyapeeth, Parbhani. It gave 11.26% and 14.39% higher oil yield than the check varieties A-1 and PBNS-12 respectively. It is recommended for Zone-I, covering Maharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh, and suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt, tolerant to Alternaria leaf spot and moderately tolerant to aphid.", "label_hi": "कुसुम PBNS-184", "label_mr": "करडई PBNS-184", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "oil_content": "11.26 and 14.39% higher oil yield over checks (A-1 and PBNS-12)", "recommended_areas_published": "Zone-I: Maharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b9a5d746-20fb-4d47-94b6-c0119a54a5cc", "maturity_days_min": 118, "maturity_days_max": 128, "yield_potential": 3.8, "yield_rainfed": 3.8, "yield_irrigated": 6.4, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "C-40-Pro.3; breeding method: Mutation breeding", "notification_number": "1178(E)", "notification_date": "2007-07-20", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PBNS-40 (Parbhani Kardi-40) is an open-pollinated safflower variety released in 2006 by the AICRP (Safflower) centre, Vasantrao Naik Marathwada Krishi Vidyapeeth, Parbhani, and notified in 2007. It was developed by mutation breeding from C-40-Pro.3. It flowers in 77-85 days and matures in 118-128 days. The plant is non-spiny. The seed oil content is 27-28%. Its potential yield under rainfed conditions is 937 kg/ha. It is recommended for all India and suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is moderately tolerant to Fusarium wilt, Alternaria leaf spot and aphid.", "label_hi": "कुसुम PBNS-40 (परभणी करडी-40)", "label_mr": "करडई PBNS-40 (परभणी करडी-40)", "aes": {"flowering_days": "77-85 days", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "oil_content": "27-28 %", "recommended_areas_published": "All India", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "118-128 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "937 kg/ha (potential) (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "652d850b-7bd4-4e12-8039-08b7e00d84d6", "maturity_days_min": 125, "maturity_days_max": 125, "yield_potential": 6.6, "yield_rainfed": 6.6, "yield_irrigated": 10.4, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Bhima x NARI-44; breeding method: Selection", "notification_number": "3482(E)", "notification_date": "2020-10-07", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Bhivara (SSF-13-71) is an open-pollinated safflower variety developed by the AICRP (Safflower) centre, Solapur, Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth, Rahuri, and notified in 2020. It was developed by selection from the cross Bhima x NARI-44. It flowers in 75-78 days and matures in 125 days. The oil content is 29.5%. Yield under rainfed conditions is 1621 kg/ha. It is recommended for Zone I (Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana and Karnataka) on medium deep to deep soils, and suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is moderately resistant to aphid, moderately tolerant to Fusarium wilt and tolerant to Alternaria leaf spot.", "label_hi": "कुसुम फुले भिवरा (SSF-13-71)", "label_mr": "करडई फुले भिवरा (SSF-13-71)", "aes": {"flowering_days": "75-78 days", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "29.5 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Zone I (Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, Telangana & Karnataka)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "125 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "1621 kg/ha (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "67f584be-403f-4370-9c35-5033dd775ba4", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 125, "yield_potential": 6.7, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Gold (SSF-15-65) is an open-pollinated safflower variety released in 2021 by the AICRP on Safflower, Solapur (MPKV, Rahuri). The crop duration is 120-125 days. Yield is 16.65 qtl./ha. The oil content is 34.6% and the oil yield is 575 kg/ha. It is recommended for safflower growing Zone-I (Maharashtra, Karnataka, Andhra and Telangana) on medium deep to deep soils. It is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt.", "label_hi": "कुसुम फुले गोल्ड (SSF-15-65)", "label_mr": "करडई फुले गोल्ड (SSF-15-65)", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "34.6 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Safflower growing Zone-I (Maharashtra, Karnataka, Andhra and Telangana)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-125 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "16.65 qtl./ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "df59cbef-add5-4e59-85c2-cf8059fbf8f5", "maturity_days_min": 125, "maturity_days_max": 130, "yield_potential": 8.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Kiran (SSF-16-02) is an open-pollinated safflower variety released in 2021 by the AICRP on Safflower, Solapur (MPKV, Rahuri). The crop duration is 125-130 days. Yield is 20.58 qtl./ha. The oil content is 30.55% and the oil yield is 632 kg/ha. It is recommended for the safflower growing areas of the country, namely Maharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh, on medium deep to deep soils. It is moderately tolerant to aphid.", "label_hi": "कुसुम फुले किरण (SSF-16-02)", "label_mr": "करडई फुले किरण (SSF-16-02)", "aes": {"soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "30.55 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Safflower growing areas of the country (Maharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "125-130 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "20.58 qtl./ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2f188886-96e3-4dbb-a5b4-2651ad78f4d9", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 125, "yield_potential": 6.9, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "Bhima x A1; hybridization followed by pedigree selection", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2020, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Nira (SSF-12-40) is an open-pollinated safflower variety released in 2020 by the AICRP on Safflower, Solapur (MPKV, Rahuri). It was developed from the cross Bhima x A1 by hybridization followed by pedigree selection. The crop duration is 120-125 days. Plants have a semi-spreading habit and the seeds are medium bold. Yield is 17 quintal/ha and oil yield is 565 kg/ha, which is 19.21% more than A1 and 13.23% more than PBNS-12. It is recommended for Maharashtra, Karnataka, Andhra and Telangana on medium deep to deep soils, and suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt and aphid.", "label_hi": "कुसुम फुले नीरा (SSF-12-40)", "label_mr": "करडई फुले नीरा (SSF-12-40)", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "565 kg/ha", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra, Karnataka, Andhra and Telangana", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120-125 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "17 quintal/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ef1af5ee-1cd6-4d08-8915-b372fd9ef31e", "maturity_days_min": 115, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 5.6, "yield_rainfed": 5.6, "yield_irrigated": 9.2, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "NARI-2 x JSI-99; breeding method: Selection", "notification_number": "2125(E)", "notification_date": "2012-09-10", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "SSF-708 is an open-pollinated safflower variety released in 2010 by the AICRP (Safflower) centre, Solapur and Mahatma Phule Krishi Vidyapeeth, Rahuri, and notified in 2012. It was developed by selection from the cross NARI-2 x JSI-99. It flowers in 68-72 days and matures in 115-120 days. The flowers are white at bloom and turn red when faded. The 100-seed weight is 5.0 g and the seed oil content is 29.1%. Yield under rainfed conditions is 1376 kg/ha. It is recommended for the safflower growing areas of Maharashtra on medium deep to deep soils, and suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is moderately tolerant to aphid.", "label_hi": "कुसुम SSF-708", "label_mr": "करडई SSF-708", "aes": {"flowering_days": "68-72 days", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "29.1 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Safflower growing areas of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "115-120 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "1376 kg/ha (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "947e69db-33aa-477c-9a3a-a325440720da", "maturity_days_min": 85, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 2.6, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "N-128 x C-50; breeding method: Pedigree", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "AKT-64 is an open-pollinated sesame variety released in 1996 by Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh Krishi Vidyapeeth, Akola (AICRP Oilseeds (Sesame), Nagpur). It was developed by the pedigree method from the cross N-128 x C-50. It is an early-maturing variety with a crop duration of 85-90 days. Plant height is 30-135 cm, with 3-4 branches and violet flowers. Seeds are dull white, with a 1000-seed weight of 3-4 gm. The oil content is 47-48%. Yield is 550-650 kg/ha. It is recommended for the kharif season in the Vidarbha region. It is resistant to Alternaria leaf spot, powdery mildew, bacterial leaf spot and wilt, moderately resistant to phyllody and Macrophomina stem/root rot, and tolerant to Phytophthora blight.", "label_hi": "तिल AKT-64", "label_mr": "तीळ AKT-64", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "oil_content": "47-48%", "recommended_areas_published": "Vidarbha region (kharif)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "85-90 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "550-650 kg/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a8b54a31-fec0-455e-97f7-d993c8234904", "maturity_days_min": 81, "maturity_days_max": 85, "yield_potential": 3.4, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "JLT-408 is an open-pollinated sesame variety released in 2010 by the Oilseeds Research Station, Jalgaon (MPKV). The crop duration is 81-85 days. It has white, bold seeds. The oil content is 53.2%, the free fatty acid content is 1.46% and the iodine value is 107. Its potential yield is 8.4 q/ha. It is recommended for the rainfed tract of Khandesh and the adjoining areas of the Vidarbha and Marathwada regions of Maharashtra, on medium to black soils, under rainfed conditions. It is moderately resistant to phyllody and Cercospora leaf spot, and tolerant to powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "तिल JLT-408", "label_mr": "तीळ JLT-408", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "soil_types": ["Medium Soil to Black Soil"], "oil_content": "53.2%", "recommended_areas_published": "Rainfed tract of Khandesh and adjoining area of Vidarbha and Marathwada region of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "81-85 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "8.4 q/ha (potential)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "36d04577-1465-4f15-af2f-3bd2bfd360ad", "maturity_days_min": 120, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 2.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "breeding method: Selection (parent not stated)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "N-8 is an open-pollinated sesame variety released in 1982 by Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh Krishi Vidyapeeth, Akola (AICRP Oilseeds (Sesame), Nagpur). It was developed by selection. It is a late-maturing variety with a crop duration of 120 days. Plant height is 110-130 cm, with 6-7 branches and violet flowers. Seeds are light brown, with a 1000-seed weight of 3-3.5 gm. The oil content is 50-51%. Yield is 400-700 kg/ha. It is recommended for the semi-rabi season in the Vidarbha zone. It is resistant to Macrophomina stem/root rot, wilt, bacterial blight, bacterial leaf spot, powdery mildew and phyllody, and tolerant to Alternaria leaf spot.", "label_hi": "तिल N-8", "label_mr": "तीळ N-8", "aes": {"oil_content": "50-51%", "recommended_areas_published": "Vidarbha zone (semi-rabi)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "400-700 kg/ha", "season_published": "semi-rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "0b5f5050-b4ef-4676-b0b1-5354c57b5c42", "maturity_days_min": 81, "maturity_days_max": 85, "yield_potential": 2.8, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "summer", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "JLT-26 x KMR 90; advance generation selection", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Phule Purna (JLT-408-2) is an open-pollinated sesame variety released in 2021 by the Oilseeds Research Station, Jalgaon (MPKV). It was developed by advance generation selection from the cross JLT-26 x KMR 90. The crop duration is 81-85 days. Seeds are bold and white, with a 1000-seed weight of 4 g. The oil content is 49.02%, the free fatty acid content is 0.81% and the iodine value is 106.8. Yield is 7 q/ha. It is recommended for summer cultivation in Khandesh and the adjoining areas of the Vidarbha and Marathwada regions, on medium to black soils. It is resistant to Cercospora leaf spot, Alternaria leaf spot, phyllody, Macrophomina stem/root rot and powdery mildew, and moderately tolerant to leaf roller and capsule borer.", "label_hi": "तिल फुले पूर्णा (JLT-408-2)", "label_mr": "तीळ फुले पूर्णा (JLT-408-2)", "aes": {"season": "summer", "soil_types": ["Medium Soil to Black Soil"], "oil_content": "49.02 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Khandesh and adjoining areas of Vidarbha and Marathwada region (summer cultivation)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "81-85 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "7 q/ha", "season_published": "summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "8bfd64d9-235c-4b71-b2a5-6a67c079bc86", "maturity_days_min": 85, "maturity_days_max": 90, "yield_potential": 5.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 2006, "variety_class": null, "description": "Bhanu is a sunflower variety released in 2006 by ZARS, Solapur (MPKV, Rahuri). The crop duration is 85-90 days. The oil content is 35-36%. Yield is 12-13 quintal/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for rainfed kharif conditions of Maharashtra on medium deep to deep soils, and it suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions. It is tolerant to drought and head borer, and moderately tolerant to sucking pests, rust, Alternaria leaf spot and sunflower necrosis disease.", "label_hi": "सूरजमुखी भानु", "label_mr": "सूर्यफूल भानु", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "35-36 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Rainfed kharif conditions of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "85-90 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "12-13 quintal/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "15ac49ec-ce93-4a98-b8fc-e6ef2440c2e8", "maturity_days_min": 80, "maturity_days_max": 85, "yield_potential": 7.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Bhaskar is a sunflower variety released in 2015 by ZARS, Solapur (MPKV, Rahuri). It is early maturing, with a crop duration of 80-85 days. Seeds are dark black and shiny. The oil content is 37-38%. Yield is 16-18 quintal/ha. It is a kharif variety recommended for rainfed kharif conditions of Maharashtra state on medium deep to deep soils, and it is suitable for the drought-prone (scarcity zone) area. It is moderately tolerant to powdery mildew, Alternaria leaf spot and sunflower necrosis disease.", "label_hi": "सूरजमुखी भास्कर", "label_mr": "सूर्यफूल भास्कर", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "37-38 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Rainfed kharif conditions of Maharashtra state; drought prone (scarcity zone) area", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "80-85 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "16-18 quintal/ha", "season_published": "kharif", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "4c5ad1ce-72df-47c1-9cbe-39ae8cfe2fb0", "maturity_days_min": 80, "maturity_days_max": 85, "yield_potential": 4.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi", "summer"], "parentage": null, "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": 1984, "variety_class": null, "description": "SS-56 is a sunflower variety released in 1984 by ZARS, Solapur (MPKV, Rahuri). The crop duration is 80-85 days. It is suitable for late sowing and for intercropping. The oil content is 32-35%. Yield is 10-11 quintal/ha. It can be grown in the kharif, rabi and summer seasons and is recommended for Maharashtra State on medium deep to deep soils under rainfed conditions. It is moderately tolerant to head borer and sucking pests.", "label_hi": "सूरजमुखी SS-56", "label_mr": "सूर्यफूल SS-56", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "soil_types": ["Medium deep to deep"], "oil_content": "32-35 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Maharashtra State", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "80-85 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "10-11 quintal/ha", "season_published": "kharif, rabi, summer", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "5407acee-de66-46f7-b28c-e1c6455ff5e7", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 6.3, "yield_rainfed": 6.3, "yield_irrigated": 8.6, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "DPC-9 x DCS-9 (Jyothi)", "notification_number": "821(E)", "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": "hybrid", "description": "DCH-177 (Deepak) is a castor hybrid released in 1999 by ICAR-IIOR, Hyderabad, Telangana, and notified under S.O. 821(E). It comes from the cross DPC-9 x DCS-9 (Jyothi). Flowering comes at 35-45 days and the first harvest at 90-100 days. Its growth habit and duration group are both medium. Plant height up to the base of the primary raceme is 150-220 cm, with 11-17 nodes up to the primary raceme. The 100-seed weight is 27.8 g and oil content is 49.0%. Yield is 1550 kg/ha under rainfed conditions. It suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions and is recommended for Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, Tamil Nadu, Karnataka and Maharashtra. It is resistant to Fusarium wilt, whitefly and lodging, and moderately tolerant to grey mould (Botrytis).", "label_hi": "अरंडी DCH-177 (दीपक)", "label_mr": "एरंड DCH-177 (दीपक)", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "90-100 days", "flowering_days": "35-45 days", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "oil_content": "49.0", "recommended_areas_published": "Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, Tamilnadu, Karnataka and Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "1550 kg/ha (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "23bf202d-35c0-45be-a98c-d8658f6c0831", "maturity_days_min": null, "maturity_days_max": null, "yield_potential": 7.7, "yield_rainfed": 7.7, "yield_irrigated": 14.5, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "JP 96 (resistant pistillate line) x DCS 89 (male line)", "notification_number": "1379(E)", "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "GCH-8 (SHB-896) is a castor hybrid released in 2018 by Sardarkrushinagar Dantiwada Agricultural University, Gujarat, and notified under S.O. 1379(E). Its parents are JP 96, a resistant pistillate line, and DCS 89, the male line. Plants branch profusely and are resistant to shattering. Yield is 18.95 q/ha under rainfed conditions. Oil content is 48.30% under rainfed and 48.60% under irrigated conditions, with oil yields of 9.15 q/ha and 16.37 q/ha respectively. It suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions and is recommended for all castor-growing states of the country. It is moderately resistant to Fusarium wilt, shows a resistant reaction to root rot (Macrophomina) with disease incidence of 20% or less, and is tolerant to lodging. Attack of semilooper, Spodoptera, leafhopper, whitefly, capsule borer and thrips is at par or somewhat less.", "label_hi": "अरंडी GCH-8 (SHB-896)", "label_mr": "एरंड GCH-8 (SHB-896)", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "oil_content": "48.30", "recommended_areas_published": "all castor growing states of the country", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"yield_published": "18.95 q/ha (rainfed)", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "80a92f01-56c5-452e-9e1d-6343b0c2eabd", "maturity_days_min": 200, "maturity_days_max": 210, "yield_potential": 15.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": 15.5, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "SKP-84 x PCS-124", "notification_number": "6318(E)", "notification_date": "2018-12-26", "release_year": 2018, "variety_class": null, "description": "GCH-9 (JHB-1018) is a castor hybrid released in 2018 by the Main Oilseeds Research Station, JAU, Junagadh, Gujarat, and notified under S.O. 6318(E) dated 2018-12-26. It comes from the cross SKP-84 x PCS-124. The first harvest comes at 110-120 days and the crop matures in 200-210 days. Its growth habit and duration group are both medium. The 100-seed weight is 28.5 g and oil content is 48.3%. Yield is 3781 kg/ha. It is recommended for irrigated areas of Gujarat. It is resistant to Fusarium wilt and root rot (Macrophomina) and tolerant to sucking pests.", "label_hi": "अरंडी GCH-9 (JHB-1018)", "label_mr": "एरंड GCH-9 (JHB-1018)", "aes": {"first_harvest_days": "110-120 days", "irrigation_regime": "irrigated", "oil_content": "48.30", "recommended_areas_published": "Gujarat (irrigated area)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "200-210 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "3781 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "be0a9169-282c-4212-97b2-42fefd2260f3", "maturity_days_min": 110, "maturity_days_max": 112, "yield_potential": 10.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "kharif", "recommended_season": ["kharif", "rabi"], "parentage": "SKP-84 (pistillate line) x DCS-94 (male line)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "GNCH-1 is a castor hybrid released in 2017 by the Pulses and Castor Research Station, Navsari Agricultural University, Navsari, Gujarat. Its parents are SKP-84, the pistillate line, and DCS-94, the male line. It matures in 110-112 days. Plants are of medium height (70-80 cm) and have a long primary spike of 64.8 cm, with 78.4 capsules per primary spike. Oil content is 47.0 to 48.0%. Yield is 2545 kg/ha. It is grown in late kharif and rabi and is recommended for south and middle Gujarat under irrigated conditions. It is resistant to Fusarium wilt and leafhopper.", "label_hi": "अरंडी GNCH-1", "label_mr": "एरंड GNCH-1", "aes": {"season": "kharif", "irrigation_regime": "irrigated", "oil_content": "47.0 to 48.0", "recommended_areas_published": "south and middle Gujarat, irrigated condition", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "110-112 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "2545 kg/ha", "season_published": "late kharif, rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "89e9ce8a-974a-4569-a5a3-d70a6a43e1b3", "maturity_days_min": 115, "maturity_days_max": 120, "yield_potential": 4.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "R-7 x RLC-4 (breeding method: Pedigree)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "NL-97 is an open-pollinated linseed variety released in 1999 by Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh Krishi Vidyapeeth, Akola, under the AICRP on Linseed. It was developed by the pedigree method from the cross R-7 x RLC-4. The crop duration is 115-120 days, in the medium maturity group. Plants are 50-55 cm tall with blue flowers. Seeds are light brown, with a 1000-seed weight of 6.89 g. Oil content is 42.1%. Yield is 800-1000 kg/ha. It is a rabi variety for rainfed conditions, recommended for the Vidarbha region of Maharashtra. It is moderately resistant to bud fly, Alternaria blight and powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "अलसी NL-97", "label_mr": "जवस NL-97", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "oil_content": "42.1", "recommended_areas_published": "Vidarbha Region of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "115-120 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "800-1000 kg/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "a96c6a82-298a-44a9-bf02-37f8223c30c6", "maturity_days_min": 97, "maturity_days_max": 111, "yield_potential": 7.3, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": "rabi", "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "R-552 x RLC-6 (breeding method: Pedigree)", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "PKV NL-260 is an open-pollinated linseed variety released in 2009 by Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh Krishi Vidyapeeth, Akola, under the AICRP on Linseed. It was developed by the pedigree method from the cross R-552 x RLC-6. The crop duration is 97-111 days, in the medium maturity group. Plants are 45-63 cm tall with blue flowers. Seeds are light brown, with a 1000-seed weight of 7.6 g. Its omega-3 content is noted as a key feature. Yield is 1100-1800 kg/ha. It is a rabi variety for rainfed or irrigated conditions, recommended for the Vidarbha region of Maharashtra. It is moderately resistant to bud fly, Alternaria blight and powdery mildew.", "label_hi": "अलसी PKV NL-260", "label_mr": "जवस PKV NL-260", "aes": {"season": "rabi", "irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "oil_content": "42.8 to 43", "recommended_areas_published": "Vidarbha Region of Maharashtra", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "97-111 days (crop duration)", "yield_published": "1100-1800 kg/ha", "season_published": "rabi", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "b06e7c47-327f-4eb6-a0a1-75d50fce377a", "maturity_days_min": 137, "maturity_days_max": 153, "yield_potential": 11.1, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "HB9908 x HB9916", "notification_number": "2815(E)", "notification_date": "2013-09-19", "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "Giriraj (DRMRIJ 31) is an open-pollinated mustard variety released in 2013 by ICAR-DRMR, Bharatpur, and notified under S.O. 2815(E) dated 2013-09-19. It comes from the cross HB9908 x HB9916. The crop matures in 137-153 days. Plants are 180-210 cm tall. The seed is bold, with a seed size of 5.6 g. Yield is 2225-2750 kg/ha. It is meant for irrigated conditions and is recommended for Zone II, which covers Delhi, Haryana, Jammu & Kashmir, Punjab and parts of Rajasthan.", "label_hi": "सरसों गिरिराज (DRMRIJ 31)", "label_mr": "मोहरी गिरिराज (DRMRIJ 31)", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "irrigated", "oil_content": "39- 42.6 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Zone II (Delhi, Haryana, Jammu & Kashmir, Punjab and parts of Rajasthan)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "137-153 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "2225-2750 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "ad12cbdf-43ea-4362-9ce9-523c03f0f9b6", "maturity_days_min": 105, "maturity_days_max": 135, "yield_potential": 6.0, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "BL 4 x Pusa Bold", "notification_number": "454(E)", "notification_date": "2009-02-11", "release_year": 2009, "variety_class": null, "description": "NRCHB 101 is an open-pollinated mustard variety released in 2009 by ICAR-DRMR, Bharatpur, and notified under S.O. 454(E) dated 2009-02-11. It comes from the cross BL 4 x Pusa Bold. The crop matures in 105-135 days. Plants are 170-200 cm tall. Seed size is 3.6-6.2 g. Oil content is 34.6-42.1%. Yield is 1382-1491 kg/ha. It suits both rainfed and irrigated conditions and is recommended for Zone III (Madhya Pradesh, Uttar Pradesh, Uttarakhand and Rajasthan) and Zone V (Bihar, Jammu & Kashmir, West Bengal, Odisha, Assam, Chhattisgarh and Manipur).", "label_hi": "सरसों NRCHB 101", "label_mr": "मोहरी NRCHB 101", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed_or_irrigated", "oil_content": "34.6- 42.1 %", "recommended_areas_published": "Zone III (M.P., U.P., Uttarakhand and Rajasthan) & Zone V (Bihar, JK, WB, Odisha, Asom, Chhattisgarh, Manipur)", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "105-135 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "1382-1491 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}, {"id": "2a9bc040-2ea6-479a-9eb3-04a1a619a8fc", "maturity_days_min": 136, "maturity_days_max": 143, "yield_potential": 10.5, "yield_rainfed": null, "yield_irrigated": null, "season": null, "recommended_season": null, "parentage": "RH 781 x RH9617", "notification_number": null, "notification_date": null, "release_year": null, "variety_class": null, "description": "RH 725 is an open-pollinated mustard variety released in 2018 by CCS HAU, Hisar. It was developed from the cross RH 781 x RH9617. The crop matures in 136-143 days. Oil content is 40.2% and yield is 2500-2600 kg/ha. It is suited to rainfed conditions and is recommended for Jammu, Punjab, Haryana, Delhi and Northern Rajasthan. It is moderately resistant to Alternaria blight, white rust and aphid.", "label_hi": "सरसों RH 725", "label_mr": "मोहरी RH 725", "aes": {"irrigation_regime": "rainfed", "oil_content": "40.2", "recommended_areas_published": "Jammu, Punjab, Haryana, Delhi and Northern Rajasthan", "source": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}, "meta": {"duration_published": "136-143 days (days to maturity)", "yield_published": "2500-2600 kg/ha", "detail_batch": "variety_detail_2026_10_03"}}]$mp$::jsonb)
  AS x(id uuid, maturity_days_min int, maturity_days_max int, yield_potential numeric, yield_rainfed numeric,
       yield_irrigated numeric, season text, recommended_season jsonb, parentage text, notification_number text,
       notification_date date, release_year int, variety_class text, description text, label_hi text, label_mr text,
       aes jsonb, meta jsonb)
)
UPDATE master_products p SET
  maturity_days_min            = CASE WHEN p.maturity_days_min IS NULL AND p.maturity_days_max IS NULL THEN x.maturity_days_min ELSE p.maturity_days_min END,
  maturity_days_max            = CASE WHEN p.maturity_days_min IS NULL AND p.maturity_days_max IS NULL THEN x.maturity_days_max ELSE p.maturity_days_max END,
  yield_potential_qtl_per_acre = COALESCE(p.yield_potential_qtl_per_acre, x.yield_potential),
  yield_rainfed_qtl_per_acre   = COALESCE(p.yield_rainfed_qtl_per_acre, x.yield_rainfed),
  yield_irrigated_qtl_per_acre = COALESCE(p.yield_irrigated_qtl_per_acre, x.yield_irrigated),
  season                       = COALESCE(NULLIF(p.season, ''), x.season),
  recommended_season           = CASE WHEN p.recommended_season IS NULL OR p.recommended_season = '[]'::jsonb
                                      THEN COALESCE(x.recommended_season, p.recommended_season) ELSE p.recommended_season END,
  parentage                    = COALESCE(NULLIF(p.parentage, ''), x.parentage),
  notification_number          = COALESCE(NULLIF(p.notification_number, ''), x.notification_number),
  notification_date            = COALESCE(p.notification_date, x.notification_date),
  release_year                 = COALESCE(p.release_year, x.release_year),
  variety_class                = COALESCE(p.variety_class, x.variety_class),
  description                  = COALESCE(NULLIF(p.description, ''), x.description),
  label_hi                     = COALESCE(NULLIF(p.label_hi, ''), x.label_hi),
  label_mr                     = COALESCE(NULLIF(p.label_mr, ''), x.label_mr),
  agro_ecological_suitability  = x.aes || COALESCE(p.agro_ecological_suitability, '{}'::jsonb),
  metadata                     = x.meta || COALESCE(p.metadata, '{}'::jsonb)
FROM x
WHERE p.id = x.id AND p.product_type = 'seed'
  AND p.metadata->>'load_batch' IN ('veg_variety_region_2026_10_03', 'pulse_oilseed_variety_region_2026_10_03');

